{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","hash":"f9062566bccbf437a1ee332d46f908c86f3f1345391540c5167c7c82a7dcd7a9","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011Y4aRmvc9CqM8nHV4rSm22","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/lcvle/lcv-workspace/.worktrees/mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers && git diff -- CHANGELOG.md README.md app/build.gradle.kts play/ | head -150","description":"Varre o diff de docs, versão e ficha da Play antes do commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B3ZZb2jEsNBBTnD18X1gvq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/lcvle/lcv-workspace/.worktrees/mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers && git diff -- backend/ | head -260","description":"Varre o diff do backend antes do commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qd3oTGBuygPchQqgeNjtJP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/lcvle/lcv-workspace/.worktrees/mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers && entire --version 2>&1 | head -2; entire session attach --help 2>&1 | head -30","description":"Confere a versão do Entire e a ajuda do comando de anexar sessão"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","hash":"67763a06d1258d915fcfecad3bd7df9b94b624025161c3ec752e6b6abc0702d0","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Y4aRmvc9CqM8nHV4rSm22","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md\nindex b600f03..31de606 100644\n--- a/CHANGELOG.md\n+++ b/CHANGELOG.md\n@@ -4,6 +4,31 @@ All material changes to Astrologo Android are recorded here.\n \n ## [Unreleased]\n \n+## [1.0.0] — 30/10/2026\n+\n+First stable release (operator decision of 30/10/2026): the first real web\n+purchase of 30/10/2026 was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20) (payment,\n+webhook, grant, generation, library, recovery on Android), and the operator\n+promoted the application to 1.0.0 for the public Play Store release.\n+\n+- Settle, instead of deferring forever, an unpaid Mercado Pago order the\n+  provider no longer knows: a definitive 4xx (not 429) on the authoritative\n+  read of a `CHECKOUT_READY` or `PAYMENT_PENDING` order with no entitlement\n+  moves it to `ABANDONED` (`manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING`, no further\n+  reread) and logs `payment_order_missing_at_provider`. The\n+  `payment_reconciliation_deferred` event added in 0.3.17 showed two\n+  test-environment orders of 27/10/2026 (`ORDTST…`) answering `404\n+  order_not_found` to the production credential and being deferred every\n+  minute since 28/10/2026. 429 and 5xx stay transient (LCV-464).\n+- Send the official SDK identification (`User-Agent: MercadoPago Java\n+  SDK/<version>`, `X-Product-Id`, `X-Tracking-Id`, the values\n+  `MercadoPagoClient` adds to every call) on every Mercado Pago request, not\n+  only on the SDK-serialized order creation; reads, cancellations, refunds,\n+  searches and chargeback lookups went out without them. Motivated by the\n+  \"SDK do backend\" recommendation on the Mercado Pago integration-quality\n+  panel (97/100 on 30/10/2026); whether the panel measures this is not\n+  documented (LCV-464).\n+\n ## [0.3.17] — 30/10/2026\n \n - Read Mercado Pago orders whose money has not settled without a paid amount:\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 660f042..c904179 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -18,10 +18,14 @@ delivery. The operator enabled commercial mode in the GCP backend on 28/10/2026;\n successful integrated generation, delivery and recovery remain unproven. This\n source does not claim a completed production acceptance or public app launch.\n \n-The **0.3.17 (versionCode 20)** candidate reads Mercado Pago orders without a\n-paid amount while no money has settled, logs each deferred reconciliation\n-item, and resolves the code-scanning alerts of 29/10/2026. It is under\n-development and has not been published. The existing approved text batch and\n+The **1.0.0 (versionCode 21)** candidate is the first stable release, by\n+operator decision of 30/10/2026: it settles unpaid Mercado Pago orders the\n+provider no longer knows instead of deferring them forever, and sends the\n+official SDK identification on every provider call. It has not been published\n+yet. **0.3.17 (versionCode 20)** was published to the\n+internal Play track on 30/10/2026 by [run 40994604713](https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/40994604713)\n+and served the first real web purchase delivered end to end (payment,\n+generation, library, Android recovery). The existing approved text batch and\n new editorial drafts have distinct review states; content presence alone is\n not proof of complete coverage or approval. Current work and evidence are in\n [LCV-464](https://linear.app/lcv-ideas-software/issue/LCV-464); web coordination\ndiff --git a/app/build.gradle.kts b/app/build.gradle.kts\nindex bca0557..aee654c 100644\n--- a/app/build.gradle.kts\n+++ b/app/build.gradle.kts\n@@ -26,8 +26,8 @@ android {\n         // operador, 04/10/2026).\n         minSdk = 36\n         targetSdk = 37\n-        versionCode = 20\n-        versionName = \"0.3.17\"\n+        versionCode = 21\n+        versionName = \"1.0.0\"\n         // Definida só por publish-play.yml (dia da publicação na Play, horário de Brasília); vazia em builds locais e de CI.\n         val publishDate = providers.gradleProperty(\"lcv.publishDate\").orNull\n         if (publishDate != null) {\ndiff --git a/play/README.md b/play/README.md\nindex 1fc2acb..bf01423 100644\n--- a/play/README.md\n+++ b/play/README.md\n@@ -1,11 +1,20 @@\n # Play listing materials\n \n These files describe **Oráculo Celestial**, package `dev.lcv.astrologo`, for its\n-Play listing. The Portuguese and English text now covers the implemented local\n-features: natal charts and complements, transits, synastry, locality maps, saved\n-history and PDF export. It explicitly keeps optional AI analysis unavailable.\n-The Portuguese and English descriptions match the native Play readback of\n-17/10/2026. A repository merge does not send these files to Play; the dated\n+Play listing. For 1.0.0 (versionCode 21), the first stable release (operator\n+decision of 30/10/2026), the Portuguese and English text presents the whole\n+product: natal chart and its readings, the free library of more than 1,800\n+element explanations, transits, synastry, locality maps, saved history and PDF\n+export, and the optional paid complete analysis prepared on the server and\n+kept in the account library (first real purchase delivered end to end on\n+30/10/2026, LCV-464). The listing text names no payment provider and no price.\n+`listings/graphics/phone/01..08.png` are the eight phone screenshots for\n+1.0.0, taken on 30/10/2026 from the real debug application on the\n+`pixel_10_api37` emulator at 1080×1920 and cropped to 1080×1800 24-bit RGB\n+(the 120 px status bar removed; within Play's two-to-one rule), in\n+Portuguese, with real local calculations for two fictitious profiles (Ana\n+Beatriz, Carlos Eduardo): home, natal wheel, planets and houses, readings,\n+free element library, transits, synastry and locality map. A repository merge does not send these files to Play; the dated\n records below identify the separate native API updates.\n \n ## Internal delivery — 0.3.15/code 18, 28/10/2026\ndiff --git a/play/listings/en-US/listing.json b/play/listings/en-US/listing.json\nindex 172d442..7bdc12a 100644\n--- a/play/listings/en-US/listing.json\n+++ b/play/listings/en-US/listing.json\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n {\n   \"language\": \"en-US\",\n   \"title\": \"Oráculo Celestial\",\n-  \"shortDescription\": \"Explore birth charts, transits and relationships. Save your history and PDFs.\",\n-  \"fullDescription\": \"Discover the elements of your birth chart and explore their connections with the sky. Oráculo Celestial brings together calculations, visual charts and information you can consult, with history stored on your device.\\n\\nBIRTH CHART AND DETAILS\\nEnter your name, birth date and time. Search for and select your birth city. View celestial positions, signs, constellations, houses and relationships between celestial bodies. You can also consult numerology, angelic and orisha correspondences, traditional elemental cycles (tatwas), planetary hours and solar information.\\n\\nTRANSITS\\nChoose a date and time to compare the sky's positions at that moment with your birth chart. Save the result and return to it later.\\n\\nCOMPARE TWO CHARTS\\nSynastry lets you compare two saved birth charts, showing relationships between celestial bodies and their positions in each person's houses.\\n\\nLOCALITY MAP\\nExplore a world map with celestial lines calculated for the moment of birth. Select the bodies you want to display and consult the calculation details and limitations.\\n\\nHISTORY AND PDF\\nReopen charts and results saved on your device. Export charts, tables and comparisons to PDF and choose where to save the file. The interface is available in Portuguese and English.\\n\\nYOUR DATA ON YOUR DEVICE\\nChart history stays on the device, with no cloud recovery library. Uninstalling the app, clearing its data or losing the device may erase that history. Keep any PDFs you want to preserve in a location of your choice.\\n\\nAI analysis is not yet available. The features described above let you calculate and explore charts without requesting that analysis.\\n\\nLCV Ideas & Software\\nSupport: suporte@lcv.dev\"\n+  \"shortDescription\": \"Birth chart, transits, synastry, locality map and a server-made full analysis.\",\n+  \"fullDescription\": \"Oráculo Celestial brings together, in one app, the precise calculation of your birth chart, free explanations of every element of the sky, and an optional complete analysis prepared on the server and delivered to your library.\\n\\nBIRTH CHART\\nEnter your name, date, time and city of birth. The app calculates the positions of the planets, signs, houses, angles and aspects with its own astronomical engine and presents everything on an interactive wheel: tap a planet, sign, house or angle to open its details. View the chart in the tropical and sidereal perspectives, consult the positions table and the complete calculation record.\\n\\nFREE READINGS AND EXPLANATIONS\\nA library of more than 1,800 articles explains planets, signs, houses, natal aspects, IAU constellations, Kabbalistic angels, orishas, numerology, tattvas and planetary hours. The texts are organised by element, searchable and sourced. Every reading of your chart opens the matching explanation.\\n\\nTRANSITS\\nChoose a date and time, or use the present moment, and compare the sky at that instant with your birth chart. Transits are saved in your history for later.\\n\\nSYNASTRY\\nCompare two saved birth charts and see the aspects between the two people's planets and each one's positions in the other's houses.\\n\\nLOCALITY MAP\\nSee, over the world map, the planetary lines calculated for the moment of birth. Choose which bodies to display, adjust the resolution and consult the details and limits of the calculation.\\n\\nHISTORY AND PDF\\nReopen charts, transits, synastries and localities saved on your device. Export charts, tables and comparisons to PDF, including a complete dossier for one person, and choose where to keep the file.\\n\\nCOMPLETE ANALYSIS\\nThe complete analysis is optional and paid. It is prepared on the server, section by section, from your chart and the additional calculations you select: transit, synastry or locality. You follow the progress per section in the app and receive a notification when the analysis is ready. Once delivered, it stays in your account's library for six months and can be opened on any device where you sign in with the same account; the PDF copy you save stays with you. The price and conditions are shown in the app before purchase.\\n\\nYOUR ACCOUNT AND YOUR DATA\\nCharts and calculations stay on your device and need no account. The account is used only for the complete analysis and the library that keeps it. Uninstalling the app or clearing its data erases the local history; the PDFs you save stay where you choose.\\n\\nThe interface is available in Portuguese and English. The app offers content for reflection and self-knowledge, not predictions.\\n\\nLCV Ideas & Software\\nSupport: suporte@lcv.dev\"\n }\ndiff --git a/play/listings/pt-BR/listing.json b/play/listings/pt-BR/listing.json\nindex b4a85a9..bc5bd27 100644\n--- a/play/listings/pt-BR/listing.json\n+++ b/play/listings/pt-BR/listing.json\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n {\n   \"language\": \"pt-BR\",\n   \"title\": \"Oráculo Celestial\",\n-  \"shortDescription\": \"Explore mapas natais, trânsitos e relações. Salve seu histórico e exporte PDF.\",\n-  \"fullDescription\": \"Conheça os elementos do seu mapa de nascimento e explore suas conexões com o céu. O Oráculo Celestial reúne cálculos, mapas visuais e informações para sua consulta, com histórico guardado no aparelho.\\n\\nMAPA NATAL E SEUS DETALHES\\nInforme nome, data e hora de nascimento. Pesquise e selecione sua cidade de nascimento. Veja a posição dos astros, signos, constelações, casas e relações entre os astros no mapa. Consulte também informações de numerologia, correspondências de anjos e orixás, ciclos tradicionais de elementos (tatwas), horas planetárias e dados do Sol.\\n\\nTRÂNSITOS\\nEscolha uma data e um horário para comparar as posições do céu daquele momento com o seu mapa natal. Salve a consulta e volte a ela depois.\\n\\nCOMPARAÇÃO ENTRE DOIS MAPAS\\nA sinastria permite comparar dois mapas natais salvos, observando relações entre os astros e suas posições nas casas de cada pessoa.\\n\\nMAPA DE LOCALIDADE\\nExplore um mapa-múndi com as linhas dos astros calculadas para o instante do nascimento. Selecione os astros que deseja visualizar e consulte os detalhes e limites do cálculo.\\n\\nHISTÓRICO E PDF\\nReabra mapas e consultas salvos no aparelho. Exporte mapas, tabelas e comparações para PDF e escolha onde guardar o arquivo. A interface está disponível em português e inglês.\\n\\nSEUS DADOS NO APARELHO\\nO histórico de mapas fica no dispositivo, sem biblioteca de recuperação em nuvem. Desinstalar o app, limpar seus dados ou perder o aparelho pode apagar esse histórico. Guarde os PDFs que deseja conservar em um local de sua escolha.\\n\\nA análise por inteligência artificial ainda não está disponível. Os recursos descritos acima permitem calcular e consultar os mapas sem solicitar essa análise.\\n\\nLCV Ideas & Software\\nSuporte: suporte@lcv.dev\"\n+  \"shortDescription\": \"Mapa natal, trânsitos, sinastria, localidade e análise completa pelo servidor.\",\n+  \"fullDescription\": \"Oráculo Celestial reúne, em um só aplicativo, o cálculo preciso do seu mapa de nascimento, explicações gratuitas de cada elemento do céu e uma análise completa opcional, preparada no servidor e entregue na sua biblioteca.\\n\\nMAPA NATAL\\nInforme nome, data, hora e cidade de nascimento. O aplicativo calcula as posições dos astros, signos, casas, ângulos e aspectos, com cálculo astronômico próprio, e apresenta tudo em uma roda interativa: toque em um planeta, signo, casa ou ângulo para abrir os detalhes. Veja o mapa nas perspectivas tropical e sideral, consulte a tabela de posições e o registro completo do cálculo.\\n\\nLEITURAS E EXPLICAÇÕES GRATUITAS\\nUma biblioteca com mais de 1.800 artigos explica planetas, signos, casas, aspectos natais, constelações da IAU, anjos cabalísticos, orixás, numerologia, tatwas e horas planetárias. Os textos são organizados por elemento, pesquisáveis e com fontes indicadas. Cada leitura do seu mapa abre a explicação correspondente.\\n\\nTRÂNSITOS\\nEscolha uma data e um horário, ou use o momento atual, e compare o céu daquele instante com o seu mapa natal. Os trânsitos ficam salvos no histórico para consulta posterior.\\n\\nSINASTRIA\\nCompare dois mapas natais salvos e observe os aspectos entre os astros das duas pessoas e as posições de cada um nas casas do outro.\\n\\nMAPA DE LOCALIDADE\\nVeja, sobre o mapa-múndi, as linhas dos astros calculadas para o instante do nascimento. Escolha os astros exibidos, ajuste a resolução e consulte os detalhes e limites do cálculo.\\n\\nHISTÓRICO E PDF\\nReabra mapas, trânsitos, sinastrias e localidades salvos no aparelho. Exporte mapas, tabelas e comparações para PDF, com dossiê completo de uma pessoa, e escolha onde guardar o arquivo.\\n\\nANÁLISE COMPLETA\\nA análise completa é opcional e paga. Ela é preparada no servidor, por seções temáticas, a partir do seu mapa e dos cálculos adicionais que você selecionar: trânsito, sinastria ou localidade. Você acompanha o progresso por seção no aplicativo e recebe uma notificação quando a análise fica pronta. Depois de entregue, ela permanece na biblioteca da sua conta por seis meses e pode ser aberta em qualquer aparelho em que você entre com a mesma conta; a cópia em PDF que você salvar permanece com você. O preço e as condições são apresentados no próprio aplicativo antes da compra.\\n\\nSUA CONTA E SEUS DADOS\\nOs mapas e cálculos ficam no aparelho e não exigem conta. A conta é usada apenas para a análise completa e para a biblioteca que a guarda. Desinstalar o aplicativo ou limpar seus dados apaga o histórico local; os PDFs que você salvar ficam onde você escolher.\\n\\nA interface está disponível em português e inglês. O aplicativo oferece conteúdo de reflexão e autoconhecimento, não previsões.\\n\\nLCV Ideas & Software\\nSuporte: suporte@lcv.dev\"\n }\ndiff --git a/play/release-notes/en-US.txt b/play/release-notes/en-US.txt\nindex 26dbf6d..cc6d51e 100644\n--- a/play/release-notes/en-US.txt\n+++ b/play/release-notes/en-US.txt\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n-0.3.17 — Fix to tracking a payment made on the web: the server now recognises orders with a pending or canceled payment and records each new check. The free explanations library, per-section progress and purchase validation are unchanged.\n+1.0.0 — First stable release of Oráculo Celestial. Natal chart with precise astronomical calculations, free explanations of every chart element, an optional complete analysis prepared on the server and delivered to your library, with per-section progress and a notice when it is ready. Purchases validated by Google Play or by Mercado Pago on the web, with the same library on all your devices.\ndiff --git a/play/release-notes/pt-BR.txt b/play/release-notes/pt-BR.txt\nindex dfe2f12..7be73c0 100644\n--- a/play/release-notes/pt-BR.txt\n+++ b/play/release-notes/pt-BR.txt\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n-0.3.17 — Correção no acompanhamento do pagamento feito pela web: o servidor passa a reconhecer pedidos com pagamento em andamento ou cancelado e registra cada nova verificação. Mantidas a biblioteca de explicações gratuitas, o progresso por seção e a validação das compras.\n+1.0.0 — Primeira versão estável do Oráculo Celestial. Mapa natal com cálculos astronômicos precisos, explicações gratuitas de cada elemento do mapa, análise completa opcional preparada no servidor e entregue na sua biblioteca, com progresso por seção e aviso quando ficar pronta. Compras validadas pelo Google Play ou pelo Mercado Pago na web, com a mesma biblioteca em todos os seus aparelhos.","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B3ZZb2jEsNBBTnD18X1gvq","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/http/v2/V2Host.kt b/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/http/v2/V2Host.kt\nindex 32d9160..50c800e 100644\n--- a/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/http/v2/V2Host.kt\n+++ b/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/http/v2/V2Host.kt\n@@ -132,6 +132,14 @@ internal class V2Resources(private val environment: Map<String, String>) : AutoC\n                     is V2Failure -> { addProperty(\"code\", failure.code); addProperty(\"detail\", failure.detail) }\n                 }\n             })\n+        }, observeMissing = { failure ->\n+            println(JsonObject().apply {\n+                addProperty(\"severity\", \"WARNING\")\n+                addProperty(\"event\", \"payment_order_missing_at_provider\")\n+                addProperty(\"channel\", \"MERCADO_PAGO\")\n+                addProperty(\"outcome\", \"ABANDONED\")\n+                failure.status?.let { addProperty(\"providerStatus\", it) }; failure.code?.let { addProperty(\"providerCode\", it) }\n+            })\n         }) }\n     private val play by lazy { PlayV2Service(FirestorePlayV2Ledger(db, store, accounts, engine),\n         NativePlayV2Gateway.fromApplicationDefaultCredentials(), engine, engine,\ndiff --git a/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/MercadoPagoOrders.kt b/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/MercadoPagoOrders.kt\nindex 2ac3390..666d121 100644\n--- a/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/MercadoPagoOrders.kt\n+++ b/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/MercadoPagoOrders.kt\n@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ package dev.lcv.astrologo.backend.payments\n \n import com.google.gson.JsonArray\n import com.google.gson.JsonObject\n+import com.mercadopago.MercadoPagoConfig\n import com.mercadopago.client.MercadoPagoClient\n import com.mercadopago.client.order.OrderCreateRequest\n import com.mercadopago.client.order.OrderConfigRequest\n@@ -265,9 +266,14 @@ internal class NativeMercadoPagoOrders(\n         if (key != null) requireHex(key)\n         val builder = HttpRequest.newBuilder(URI(\"https://api.mercadopago.com$path\"))\n             .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(8)).header(\"Authorization\", authorization).header(\"Accept\", \"application/json\")\n+            // The same identification the official SDK puts on every call (MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders),\n+            // so reads, cancellations and refunds carry it like the SDK-serialized creation already did.\n+            .setHeader(Headers.USER_AGENT, \"MercadoPago Java SDK/${MercadoPagoConfig.CURRENT_VERSION}\")\n+            .setHeader(Headers.PRODUCT_ID, MercadoPagoConfig.PRODUCT_ID)\n+            .setHeader(Headers.TRACKING_ID, MercadoPagoConfig.TRACKING_ID)\n         if (key != null) builder.header(\"X-Idempotency-Key\", key)\n         if (body != null) builder.header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json; charset=utf-8\")\n-        sdkHeaders.forEach { (name, value) -> builder.header(name, value) }\n+        sdkHeaders.forEach { (name, value) -> builder.setHeader(name, value) }\n         builder.method(method, if (body == null) HttpRequest.BodyPublishers.noBody()\n             else HttpRequest.BodyPublishers.ofString(body.toString(), Charsets.UTF_8))\n         return try {\ndiff --git a/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt b/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\nindex 366eda7..b6ba797 100644\n--- a/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\n+++ b/backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\n@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@ internal class UniversalOrderService(\n     private val registrationDate: (FirebaseAccountVerification.Verified) -> Instant? = { null },\n     /** Called once per reconciliation item the sweep defers (item kind, provider or contract failure). */\n     private val observeDeferral: (String, Exception) -> Unit = { _, _ -> },\n+    /** Called once per unpaid order the provider no longer knows (4xx on the authoritative read). */\n+    private val observeMissing: (MpUnavailable) -> Unit = { },\n ) {\n     // Firestore persists timestamps to microseconds; CAS snapshots must use that same precision.\n     private val clock = Clock.tick(clock, Duration.ofNanos(1_000))\n@@ -326,7 +328,19 @@ internal class UniversalOrderService(\n                         }\n                     }\n                     order.state in setOf(UniversalOrderState.CHECKOUT_READY, UniversalOrderState.PAYMENT_PENDING) && order.mpOrderId != null -> {\n-                        val fresh = provider.read(order.mpOrderId)\n+                        val fresh = try { provider.read(order.mpOrderId) } catch (failure: MpUnavailable) {\n+                            // A definitive 4xx (not 429) on the authoritative resource: the provider does not know\n+                            // this order under this credential (test-environment orders read with the production\n+                            // token, for example). Nothing was granted, so deferring it forever only costs a\n+                            // provider call per minute. Settle it instead of retrying (LCV-464, 30/10/2026).\n+                            if (failure.status !in 400..499 || failure.status == 429 || order.entitlement != UniversalEntitlement.NONE) throw failure\n+                            observeMissing(failure)\n+                            store.mutate(order.orderReference) { saved, _ ->\n+                                if (saved != order) saved else saved.copy(state = UniversalOrderState.ABANDONED,\n+                                    subjectName = null, nextRereadAt = null, manualCase = \"PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING\")\n+                            }\n+                            return@reconcileItem\n+                        }\n                         observeAuthoritative(order.mpOrderId, fresh)\n                         if (order.checkoutExpiresAt != null && now >= order.checkoutExpiresAt.plusSeconds(86_400) &&\n                             fresh.status in setOf(\"created\", \"action_required\", \"processing\")) provider.cancel(order.mpOrderId)\ndiff --git a/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/NativeMercadoPagoOrdersTest.kt b/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/NativeMercadoPagoOrdersTest.kt\nindex ce3c153..60a8ec2 100644\n--- a/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/NativeMercadoPagoOrdersTest.kt\n+++ b/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/NativeMercadoPagoOrdersTest.kt\n@@ -206,6 +206,27 @@ class NativeMercadoPagoOrdersTest {\n         assertEquals(listOf(\"GET /users/me\", \"POST /v1/orders\", \"POST /v1/orders\"), http.calls)\n         assertEquals(listOf(\"b\".repeat(64), \"d\".repeat(64)), sentKeys)\n     }\n+    @Test fun everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification() {\n+        val seen = mutableMapOf<String, Map<String, String>>()\n+        val http = StubHttpClient { request ->\n+            seen[request.uri().path] = listOf(\"User-Agent\", \"X-Product-Id\", \"X-Tracking-Id\").associateWith { request.headers().firstValue(it).orElse(\"\") }\n+            when (request.uri().path) {\n+                \"/users/me\" -> 200 to \"\"\"{\"id\":12345,\"site_id\":\"MLB\",\"tags\":[\"test_user\"]}\"\"\"\n+                \"/v1/orders/ORDTST123\" -> 200 to orderJson\n+                \"/v1/orders/ORDTST123/cancel\" -> 200 to \"{}\"\n+                else -> error(\"Unexpected provider request\")\n+            }\n+        }\n+        val provider = NativeMercadoPagoOrders(\"fixture-token\", config, http = http)\n+        provider.read(\"ORDTST123\"); provider.cancel(\"ORDTST123\")\n+        assertEquals(setOf(\"/users/me\", \"/v1/orders/ORDTST123\", \"/v1/orders/ORDTST123/cancel\"), seen.keys)\n+        for ((path, headers) in seen) {\n+            assertEquals(path, \"MercadoPago Java SDK/${com.mercadopago.MercadoPagoConfig.CURRENT_VERSION}\", headers.getValue(\"User-Agent\"))\n+            assertEquals(path, com.mercadopago.MercadoPagoConfig.PRODUCT_ID, headers.getValue(\"X-Product-Id\"))\n+            assertEquals(path, com.mercadopago.MercadoPagoConfig.TRACKING_ID, headers.getValue(\"X-Tracking-Id\"))\n+            assertTrue(path, headers.getValue(\"X-Tracking-Id\").startsWith(\"platform:\"))\n+        }\n+    }\n     @Test fun misboundLiveOrDifferentSellerCredentialCannotCreateAnyOrder() {\n         for (body in listOf(\n             \"\"\"{\"id\":12345,\"site_id\":\"MLB\",\"tags\":[\"normal\"]}\"\"\",\ndiff --git a/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt b/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt\nindex d6ed5cf..9eba40e 100644\n--- a/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt\n+++ b/backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt\n@@ -96,7 +96,8 @@ private class Fixture {\n             addProperty(\"state\", order.generationState); addProperty(\"completedSteps\", 0); addProperty(\"totalSteps\", 0)\n             add(\"progress\", JsonNull.INSTANCE); add(\"updatedAt\", JsonNull.INSTANCE)\n         } }, Clock.fixed(serviceNow, ZoneOffset.UTC),\n-        observeDeferral = { kind, failure -> deferrals += \"$kind:${failure.javaClass.simpleName}\" })\n+        observeDeferral = { kind, failure -> deferrals += \"$kind:${failure.javaClass.simpleName}\" },\n+        observeMissing = { failure -> deferrals += \"MISSING:${failure.status}:${failure.code}\" })\n     val principal = FirebaseAccountVerification.Verified(\"b\".repeat(64), \"synthetic-firebase-uid\", \"google.com\", serviceNow.epochSecond,\n         verifiedEmail = \"buyer@example.invalid\")\n     fun seed(order: UniversalOrder = fixtureOrder()) { store.rows[order.orderReference] = order; store.bindings[requireNotNull(order.mpOrderId)] = order.orderReference to true; provider.rows[order.mpOrderId] = provider.row(order.orderReference) }\n@@ -251,6 +252,29 @@ class UniversalOrderServiceTest {\n         }\n     }\n \n+    @Test fun unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever() {\n+        // Two test-environment orders of 27/10/2026 answered 404 order_not_found to the production credential and\n+        // were deferred every minute from 28/10 to 30/10 (LCV-464).\n+        val f = Fixture(); val order = fixtureOrder().copy(nextRereadAt = serviceNow); f.seed(order)\n+        f.provider.onRead = { throw MpUnavailable(404, \"order_not_found\") }\n+        val result = f.service.reconcileSweep()\n+        assertEquals(1, result.get(\"reconciled\").asInt); assertEquals(0, result.get(\"unavailable\").asInt)\n+        val saved = f.store.rows.getValue(fixtureHash)\n+        assertEquals(UniversalOrderState.ABANDONED, saved.state); assertNull(saved.nextRereadAt); assertNull(saved.subjectName)\n+        assertEquals(\"PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING\", saved.manualCase); assertEquals(UniversalEntitlement.NONE, saved.entitlement)\n+        assertEquals(listOf(\"MISSING:404:order_not_found\"), f.deferrals)\n+        assertEquals(0, f.provider.refunds)\n+        // 429 and 5xx stay transient: deferred, untouched.\n+        for (status in listOf(429, 500, 503)) {\n+            val g = Fixture(); g.seed(order)\n+            g.provider.onRead = { throw MpUnavailable(status) }\n+            assertEquals(1, g.service.reconcileSweep().get(\"unavailable\").asInt)\n+            assertEquals(UniversalOrderState.CHECKOUT_READY, g.store.rows.getValue(fixtureHash).state)\n+            assertEquals(serviceNow.plusSeconds(60), g.store.rows.getValue(fixtureHash).nextRereadAt)\n+            assertEquals(listOf(\"ORDER:MpUnavailable\"), g.deferrals)\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n     @Test fun failedUnboundCaseDoesNotOverwriteConcurrentSettlementScheduleOrAttempt() {\n         val original = UnboundMpRefund(\"case\", fixtureHash, \"UNBOUND\", 0, 0, \"REFUND_DUE\",\n             serviceNow, financialUntil(serviceNow))","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qd3oTGBuygPchQqgeNjtJP","type":"tool_result","content":"Entire CLI 0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1+idle-fallback.2\nGo version: go1.27.3\nAttach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit, or to the commit named by --commit. Use this when hooks failed\nto fire or weren't installed when the session started, or to attach a\nresearch session.\n\nHow the session is linked follows from two facts about the commit — does it\nalready have a checkpoint, and is it pushed — the same for HEAD and --commit:\n  - It already has a checkpoint: the session is added to it. Git history is\n    not changed.\n  - It is already pushed: the commit is left unchanged and the link is\n    recorded in a new checkpoint, which is pushed right away. The link counts\n    once the commit's author attaches it, and names that exact commit: after\n    a rebase or amend, attach the session to the new commit.\n  - It isn't pushed: the Entire-Checkpoint trailer is added to it, which\n    rewrites it and any commits after it on the current branch (their content\n    is unchanged). A trailer survives a later rebase. Merges after the commit,\n    or a rebase or merge in progress, are refused. If a remote can't be\n    reached to confirm the commit isn't pushed, attach refuses rather than\n    risk rewriting a shared commit.\n\nattach prints what it is about to do and asks before doing it. Without a\nterminal (an agent or a script) it changes nothing and exits non-zero; show\nthe user what it printed, and once they agree, rerun with --force.\n\nA session can be attached to more than one commit. Each checkpoint records the\nturns since the session's previous checkpoint.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The","is_error":false}]}}
