{"parentUuid":"093ea477-9a65-4271-9f63-3f4428b4602e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-mythos-5-1","id":"msg_011CgXnffuKuAzvD8kPJ4b26","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015wSANDDKpKfG6MWTZC9zbc","name":"mcp__github__pull_request_read","input":{"method":"get_review_comments","owner":"LCV-Ideas-Software","repo":"astrologo-android","pullNumber":170},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1069,"cache_read_input_tokens":282390,"output_tokens":488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1069,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":282390,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1069},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015wSANDDKpKfG6MWTZC9zbc":{"method":"get_review_comments","owner":"LCV-Ideas-Software","repo":"astrologo-android","pullNumber":170}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgXnff4j8Eqy1YgLfohpx","requestRef":"1019f064-f831-4b64-8a61-d4b0f8e42832","requestedModel":"claude-mythos-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba34cc2e-a9cb-4e93-8dc7-07b3569f3747","timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:26:38.440Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\github-operations","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
{"parentUuid":"ba34cc2e-a9cb-4e93-8dc7-07b3569f3747","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"15cf841e-2aaa-49fe-9d73-7511af69f2d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015wSANDDKpKfG6MWTZC9zbc","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"pageInfo\":{\"endCursor\":\"REDACTED\",\"hasNextPage\":false,\"hasPreviousPage\":false,\"startCursor\":\"REDACTED\"},\"review_threads\":[{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict abandonment to confirmed missing-resource errors**\\n\\nIf the Mercado Pago credential becomes invalid or loses permission, `provider.read()` propagates a 401/403 as `MpUnavailable`, and this condition abandons every due unpaid order it encounters. Those responses do not establish that the orders are missing. Clearing `nextRereadAt` prevents reconciliation from resuming after credentials are repaired; moreover, a later accredited webhook reaches `MpOrderTransitions.observe()` with an `ABANDONED` order, which triggers `NOT_GRANTABLE` and a refund instead of delivery. Only abandon orders on a confirmed missing-resource response, such as the intended `404 order_not_found`, and continue deferring authentication and other unrelated 4xx failures.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:19Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/pull/170#discussion_r4420424886\",\"line\":340,\"original_line\":340,\"original_start_line\":336,\"path\":\"backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\",\"start_line\":336,\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:19Z\"}],\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOUDH-s86x2GDh\",\"is_collapsed\":false,\"is_outdated\":false,\"is_resolved\":false,\"total_count\":1},{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"claude\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Credential/authorization 4xx abandons every pending order, and later payments get auto-refunded**\\n\\nThe guard treats any 4xx except 429 as \\\"the provider no longer knows this order\\\". That includes 401 (a revoked, rotated or misbound token) and 403 (for example the `PA_UNAUTHORIZED` 403 already seen from the Orders API in LCV-483), and also 400. Those failures come from our credential, not from the order. If one happens, a single sweep moves every due `CHECKOUT_READY`/`PAYMENT_PENDING` order to `ABANDONED` with `nextRereadAt = null`. Nothing cancels the checkout at Mercado Pago, so a buyer can still pay it. When that payment's webhook arrives, `MpOrderTransitions.observe` returns `NOT_GRANTABLE` for `ABANDONED`, so the paid order goes to `REFUND_DUE` and the buyer gets a refund instead of the analysis. Fix: limit the settlement to the case the PR actually saw, a 404 (ideally with `code == \\\"order_not_found\\\"`), and keep 400/401/403 transient so they are deferred and logged.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n                            if (failure.status != 404 || failure.code != \\\"order_not_found\\\" || order.entitlement != UniversalEntitlement.NONE) throw failure\\n```\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/pull/170#discussion_r4420426283\",\"line\":336,\"original_line\":336,\"path\":\"backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:39Z\"}],\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOUDH-s86x2GQs\",\"is_collapsed\":false,\"is_outdated\":false,\"is_resolved\":false,\"total_count\":1}],\"totalCount\":2}"}]},"uuid":"691b67c5-598f-4194-b24d-d3b253fd9fae","timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:26:39.452Z","toolUseResult":"{\"pageInfo\":{\"endCursor\":\"REDACTED\",\"hasNextPage\":false,\"hasPreviousPage\":false,\"startCursor\":\"REDACTED\"},\"review_threads\":[{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict abandonment to confirmed missing-resource errors**\\n\\nIf the Mercado Pago credential becomes invalid or loses permission, `provider.read()` propagates a 401/403 as `MpUnavailable`, and this condition abandons every due unpaid order it encounters. Those responses do not establish that the orders are missing. Clearing `nextRereadAt` prevents reconciliation from resuming after credentials are repaired; moreover, a later accredited webhook reaches `MpOrderTransitions.observe()` with an `ABANDONED` order, which triggers `NOT_GRANTABLE` and a refund instead of delivery. Only abandon orders on a confirmed missing-resource response, such as the intended `404 order_not_found`, and continue deferring authentication and other unrelated 4xx failures.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\n\\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:19Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/pull/170#discussion_r4420424886\",\"line\":340,\"original_line\":340,\"original_start_line\":336,\"path\":\"backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\",\"start_line\":336,\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:19Z\"}],\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOUDH-s86x2GDh\",\"is_collapsed\":false,\"is_outdated\":false,\"is_resolved\":false,\"total_count\":1},{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"claude\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Credential/authorization 4xx abandons every pending order, and later payments get auto-refunded**\\n\\nThe guard treats any 4xx except 429 as \\\"the provider no longer knows this order\\\". That includes 401 (a revoked, rotated or misbound token) and 403 (for example the `PA_UNAUTHORIZED` 403 already seen from the Orders API in LCV-483), and also 400. Those failures come from our credential, not from the order. If one happens, a single sweep moves every due `CHECKOUT_READY`/`PAYMENT_PENDING` order to `ABANDONED` with `nextRereadAt = null`. Nothing cancels the checkout at Mercado Pago, so a buyer can still pay it. When that payment's webhook arrives, `MpOrderTransitions.observe` returns `NOT_GRANTABLE` for `ABANDONED`, so the paid order goes to `REFUND_DUE` and the buyer gets a refund instead of the analysis. Fix: limit the settlement to the case the PR actually saw, a 404 (ideally with `code == \\\"order_not_found\\\"`), and keep 400/401/403 transient so they are deferred and logged.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n                            if (failure.status != 404 || failure.code != \\\"order_not_found\\\" || order.entitlement != UniversalEntitlement.NONE) throw failure\\n```\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/pull/170#discussion_r4420426283\",\"line\":336,\"original_line\":336,\"path\":\"backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:39Z\"}],\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOUDH-s86x2GQs\",\"is_collapsed\":false,\"is_outdated\":false,\"is_resolved\":false,\"total_count\":1}],\"totalCount\":2}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"github-mcp-server","title":"GitHub MCP Server","icons":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,REDACTED","mimeType":"image/png","theme":"light"},{"src":"data:image/png;base64,REDACTED","mimeType":"image/png","theme":"dark"}],"version":"github-mcp-server/remote-59427b793443f88795375c20cd01d8e035ecca69"}},"structuredContent":{"pageInfo":{"endCursor":"REDACTED","hasNextPage":false,"hasPreviousPage":false,"startCursor":"REDACTED"},"review_threads":[{"comments":[{"author":"chatgpt-codex-connector","body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict abandonment to confirmed missing-resource errors**\n\nIf the Mercado Pago credential becomes invalid or loses permission, `provider.read()` propagates a 401/403 as `MpUnavailable`, and this condition abandons every due unpaid order it encounters. Those responses do not establish that the orders are missing. Clearing `nextRereadAt` prevents reconciliation from resuming after credentials are repaired; moreover, a later accredited webhook reaches `MpOrderTransitions.observe()` with an `ABANDONED` order, which triggers `NOT_GRANTABLE` and a refund instead of delivery. Only abandon orders on a confirmed missing-resource response, such as the intended `404 order_not_found`, and continue deferring authentication and other unrelated 4xx failures.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:24:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/pull/170#discussion_r4420424886","line":340,"original_line":340,"original_start_line":336,"path":"backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt","start_line":336,"updated_at":"2026-10-30T04:24:19Z"}],"id":"PRRT_kwDOUDH-s86x2GDh","is_collapsed":false,"is_outdated":false,"is_resolved":false,"total_count":1},{"comments":[{"author":"claude","body":"**<sub><sub>![](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Credential/authorization 4xx abandons every pending order, and later payments get auto-refunded**\n\nThe guard treats any 4xx except 429 as \"the provider no longer knows this order\". That includes 401 (a revoked, rotated or misbound token) and 403 (for example the `PA_UNAUTHORIZED` 403 already seen from the Orders API in LCV-483), and also 400. Those failures come from our credential, not from the order. If one happens, a single sweep moves every due `CHECKOUT_READY`/`PAYMENT_PENDING` order to `ABANDONED` with `nextRereadAt = null`. Nothing cancels the checkout at Mercado Pago, so a buyer can still pay it. When that payment's webhook arrives, `MpOrderTransitions.observe` returns `NOT_GRANTABLE` for `ABANDONED`, so the paid order goes to `REFUND_DUE` and the buyer gets a refund instead of the analysis. Fix: limit the settlement to the case the PR actually saw, a 404 (ideally with `code == \"order_not_found\"`), and keep 400/401/403 transient so they are deferred and logged.\n\n```suggestion\n                            if (failure.status != 404 || failure.code != \"order_not_found\" || order.entitlement != UniversalEntitlement.NONE) throw failure\n```","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:24:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/pull/170#discussion_r4420426283","line":336,"original_line":336,"path":"backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt","updated_at":"2026-10-30T04:24:39Z"}],"id":"PRRT_kwDOUDH-s86x2GQs","is_collapsed":false,"is_outdated":false,"is_resolved":false,"total_count":1}],"totalCount":2}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba34cc2e-a9cb-4e93-8dc7-07b3569f3747","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\github-operations","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
