{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","hash":"77a29762c01585dafbd450e114a2d824aa560b71abadbbd1c7b36144bd888445","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DKHtS2bwooBVBz2LHr7o9p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/lcvle/lcv-workspace/.worktrees/mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers && entire trail --help 2>&1 | sed -n '1,40p'","description":"Lista os subcomandos de trail do Entire"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vp9xDKzf6sHTjpeiQycCGA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/lcvle/lcv-workspace/.worktrees/mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers && sed -n '290,305p' backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/payments/MercadoPagoOrders.kt | cut -c1-200; grep -n 'onRead\\|class FakeProvider\\|MpUnavailable(' backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt | head -8 | cut -c1-160","description":"Lê como o código do erro é extraído e como o teste simula o provedor"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","hash":"1ea5c889025c6ec7ae6f7e83a9dafbe03da7352231dcac988c7ea141b187aac6","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DKHtS2bwooBVBz2LHr7o9p","type":"tool_result","content":"A trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vp9xDKzf6sHTjpeiQycCGA","type":"tool_result","content":"            // Also bound completion explicitly: a timeout at headers alone must not leave body reads open.\n            val pending = http.sendAsync(builder.build(), handler)\n            val response = try { pending.get(8, TimeUnit.SECONDS) }\n                catch (failure: Exception) { pending.cancel(true); throw failure }\n            val bytes = response.body()\n            val objectBody = try { V2HttpBoundary.strictObject(bytes) } catch (_: Exception) { throw MpUnavailable(response.statusCode()) }\n            if (response.statusCode() !in accepted) {\n                val code = sequenceOf(objectBody.get(\"code\"), objectBody.getAsJsonArray(\"errors\")?.firstOrNull()?.asJsonObject?.get(\"code\"))\n                    .filterNotNull().firstOrNull()?.takeIf { it.isJsonPrimitive }?.asString\n                    ?.takeIf { it.matches(Regex(\"[a-z0-9_]{1,96}\")) }\n                val retryAfter = response.headers().firstValue(\"Retry-After\").orElse(null)?.toLongOrNull()?.takeIf { it >= 0 }\n                throw MpUnavailable(response.statusCode(), code, retryAfter)\n            }\n            objectBody\n        } catch (failure: MpUnavailable) { throw failure }\n          catch (interrupted: InterruptedException) { Thread.currentThread().interrupt(); throw MpUnavailable() }\n63:    var onRead: (String) -> Unit = {}\n77:        failCreateStatus?.let { throw MpUnavailable(it) }\n78:        if (failCreateOnce) { failCreateOnce = false; throw MpUnavailable() }\n82:    override fun read(id: String): MpOrder { reads++; onRead(id); return rows[id] ?: throw MpUnavailable(404) }\n157:            f.provider.onRead = {\n168:        for (failure in listOf(MpUnavailable(429, retryAfterSeconds = 7200),\n169:            MpUnavailable(400, \"cannot_refund_order\"), MpUnavailable(409, \"idempotency_key_already_used\"))) {\n206:        f.provider.onSearch = { throw MpUnavailable(503) }","is_error":false}]}}
