{"parentUuid":"39d09d16-b1f6-4dc9-b770-a43a3afd7f24","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"15cf841e-2aaa-49fe-9d73-7511af69f2d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNFusYHPbq5oZMKigJqL72","type":"tool_result","content":"Show a finding\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding show [<trail>] <finding-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for show\n\n=== 01M65GSE4YNW5XJ0RC8XD84GRR\nUsing context 'google-104751472848289018033@br.auth.entire.io'.\nFinding:   01M65GSE4YNW5XJ0RC8XD84GRR\nStatus:    open\nFreshness: current\nSeverity:  low\nConfidence: 0.60\nLocation: backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt:255-276\n\nThe test proves only that 404 settles and that 429/500/503 defer. It never checks 401/403/400, which the new rule also settles, so the most dangerous branch of the new behavior has no test. Add assertions for the auth/validation statuses, and make them defer once the rule is narrowed.\n=== 01M65GVDG7XPWNQTXMT82GJC1D\nUsing context 'google-104751472848289018033@br.auth.entire.io'.\nFinding:   01M65GVDG7XPWNQTXMT82GJC1D\nStatus:    open\nFreshness: current\nSeverity:  medium\nConfidence: 0.98\nLocation: backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt:336-340\n\nA 401/403 caused by expired credentials or denied access also reaches this branch: `MercadoPagoOrders.kt:205,295–301` propagates those HTTP failures without distinguishing them from missing orders. The sweep permanently abandons valid checkouts and removes their retries; after credentials recover, an accredited webhook causes a `NOT_GRANTABLE` refund instead of fulfillment (`UniversalOrderService.kt:451–457`). Restrict abandonment to verified missing-order responses and defer authentication and other unrelated 4xx failures.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"553c6532-e693-4370-bd46-9694bda0fbcd","timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:28:46.894Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Show a finding\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding show [<trail>] <finding-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for show\n\n=== 01M65GSE4YNW5XJ0RC8XD84GRR\nUsing context 'google-104751472848289018033@br.auth.entire.io'.\nFinding:   01M65GSE4YNW5XJ0RC8XD84GRR\nStatus:    open\nFreshness: current\nSeverity:  low\nConfidence: 0.60\nLocation: backend/src/test/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderServiceTest.kt:255-276\n\nThe test proves only that 404 settles and that 429/500/503 defer. It never checks 401/403/400, which the new rule also settles, so the most dangerous branch of the new behavior has no test. Add assertions for the auth/validation statuses, and make them defer once the rule is narrowed.\n=== 01M65GVDG7XPWNQTXMT82GJC1D\nUsing context 'google-104751472848289018033@br.auth.entire.io'.\nFinding:   01M65GVDG7XPWNQTXMT82GJC1D\nStatus:    open\nFreshness: current\nSeverity:  medium\nConfidence: 0.98\nLocation: backend/src/main/kotlin/dev/lcv/astrologo/backend/universalorders/UniversalOrderService.kt:336-340\n\nA 401/403 caused by expired credentials or denied access also reaches this branch: `MercadoPagoOrders.kt:205,295–301` propagates those HTTP failures without distinguishing them from missing orders. The sweep permanently abandons valid checkouts and removes their retries; after credentials recover, an accredited webhook causes a `NOT_GRANTABLE` refund instead of fulfillment (`UniversalOrderService.kt:451–457`). Restrict abandonment to verified missing-order responses and defer authentication and other unrelated 4xx failures.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39d09d16-b1f6-4dc9-b770-a43a3afd7f24","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.