plicable laws and regulations relating to children. Examples include the US Children's Online Privacy Protection Act COPPA, and the EU General Data Protection \r\n[read] DK code in the app uses advertising ID. If so, it must be declared that the app uses it. Some SDKs, such as the Google Mobile Ads SDK (Play Services-ads) may already declare the `com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID` permission in the SDK's library manifest. If the app uses these SDKs as dependencies, the `com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID` permissi\r\n[submit] uired. - **Question ID:** `POLICY_QUESTION_ID_NEWS_MAGS_SUBMITTER_ENTITY_NAME`   - **Type:** String   - **Question Text:** Provide the name of the entity being submitted on behalf of.   - **Conditions:** Required if `POLICY_QUESTION_ID_NEWS_MAGS_SUBMITTING_FOR_LEGAL_ENTITY` is false. - **Question ID:** `POLICY_QUESTION_ID_NEWS_MAGS_ENTITY_CONTACT_URL`   - **","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9094119f-d08b-44ad-9f90-43a53ad6b931","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
{"parentUuid":"dfc68ab9-1fa1-4b26-b4a0-1d19fed38ea0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-mythos-5-1","id":"msg_011CgXppKYDcEUg2wPH8jM6b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ASVzNUeyrJV4pj1PpjWary","name":"mcp__google-dev-docs__search_documents","input":{"query":"androidpublisher v3 appstorereview policy declarations API submit app for review REST resource"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9631,"cache_read_input_tokens":431912,"output_tokens":1448,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":458},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9631,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1448,"cache_read_input_tokens":431912,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9631},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ASVzNUeyrJV4pj1PpjWary":{"query":"androidpublisher v3 appstorereview policy declarations API submit app for review REST resource"}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgXppK7An56dBVbSAqj8X","requestRef":"d3d1ff4d-55a5-4dfa-9383-9c3eabf9da74","requestedModel":"claude-mythos-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"62430775-ce5d-483b-ba51-ff7439d843d5","timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:55:09.531Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
{"parentUuid":"62430775-ce5d-483b-ba51-ff7439d843d5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca7f7a62-2c98-4c13-acad-efff44eb1c51","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ASVzNUeyrJV4pj1PpjWary","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"results\":[{\"content\":\"### Policy Declarations\\n\\nWhen submitting or updating app information using the API, you must include any required policy declarations.Declaration RequirementsThe following declarations are in scope: Required for all apps to confirm if additional declarations are needed:\\n\\n* Health Apps: Tell us what health features the app uses to help us to understand which requirements the app must meet in the Health apps policy.\\n* Financial Features: Apps that provide financial features might need to comply with certain regulations in some countries or regions. Submit accurate and up-to-date details of the financial features in the app to help us make sure the right teams review the submission.\\n* Advertising ID: Help us understand whether the app uses advertising ID.\\n* Testing Credentials (Sign in details): If any part of the app is restricted based on sign in details, memberships, location, or other forms of authentication, provide instructions on how to access them.\\n* Privacy Policy: A link to and details about the app's privacy policy.\\n* Target Audience and Content: You must let us know the target age group of the app, and other information about its contents. This helps make sure that apps designed for children are safe and appropriate.\\n* Ads: You must let us know whether the app contains ads.\\n\\nConditionally Required:\\n\\n* Government Apps: Tell us if the app is for use by a government of any kind. This includes national, state and city governments, and local authorities. This helps us to make sure the right teams review the submission. If this declaration is not completed, the app will be considered not a government app.\\n* Child Safety Standards: Required for apps in the \\\"Social\\\" or \\\"Dating\\\" categories. Apps in the social or dating categories must provide published safety standards and contact information to comply with our\\n[child safety standards policy](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/14747720).\\n* News and Magazine Apps: Required for apps in the \\\"News and Magazines\\\" category. Add details about the news and magazine app to provide transparency about the entities behind the app.\\n\\nNote: Refer to the\\n[detailed guide](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations)to get a complete overview of each declaration, including question IDs, choice IDs, and examples.API Request StructurePolicy declarations are provided within the policyDeclarations array in the body of the\\n[UpdateAppStoreHostedAppRequest](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/api-ref/rest/v3/appstoreappsreview/updateappstorehostedapp). Each item in this array is an AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration object. AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration Object:\\n\\n* declarationId (string, Required): The unique identifier for the policy declaration (e.g., POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_FINANCE , POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT ).\\n* responses (Array of PolicyResponse , Required): A list of answers to the questions within that specific declaration.\\n\\nPolicyResponse Object:\",\"id\":\"c3\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review\"},{\"content\":\"## 2. Advertising ID Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADVERTISING_ID\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_IS_USED\\n\\n    * Type: Boolean\\n    * Question Text: Does the app use advertising ID? This includes any SDKs that the app imports that use advertising ID.\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_PURPOSE\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: Why does the app need to use advertising ID? This includes any SDKs the app imports that use advertising IDs. When this question is answered, make sure to verify if any third-party SDK code in the app uses advertising ID. If so, it must be declared that the app uses it. Some SDKs, such as the Google Mobile Ads SDK (Play Services-ads) may already declare the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission in the SDK's library manifest. If the app uses these SDKs as dependencies, the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission from the SDK's library manifest will be merged with the app's main manifest by default, even if the permission is not explicitly declared.\\n[Learn more](https://developer.android.com/studio/build/manage-manifests#merge-manifests).\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * App functionality ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_APP_FUNCTIONALITY )\\n\\n            * Used for features in the app. For example, to enable functionality, or authenticate users.\\n\\n\\n        * Analytics ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ANALYTICS )\\n\\n            * Used to collect data about how users use the app, or how the app performs. For example, to see how many users are using a particular feature, to monitor app health, to diagnose and fix bugs or crashes, or to make future performance improvements.\\n\\n\\n        * Developer communications ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_DEVELOPER_COMMUNICATIONS )\\n\\n            * Used to send news or notifications about the developer or the app. For example, sending a push notification to inform users about an important security update, or informing users about new features in the app.\\n\\n\\n        * Fraud prevention, security, and compliance ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_FRAUD_PREVENTION_SECURITY )\\n\\n            * Used for fraud prevention, security, or compliance with laws. For example, monitoring failed login attempts to identify possible fraudulent activity.\\n\\n\\n        * Advertising or marketing ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ADVERTISING )\\n\\n            * Used to display or target ads or marketing communications, or measure ad performance. For example, displaying ads in the app, sending push notifications to promote other products or services, or sharing data with advertising partners.\\n\\n\\n        * Personalization ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_PERSONALIZATION )\\n\\n            * Used to customize the app, such as showing recommended content or suggestions. For example, suggesting playlists based on users' listening habits, or delivering local news based on a user's location.\\n\\n\\n        * Account management ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT )\\n\\n            * Used for the setup or management of user accounts. For example, to enable users to create accounts; to add information to accounts provided for use across services; to log in to the app; or to verify their credentials.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_IS_USED is true.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_ACK\\n\\n    * Type: Boolean\\n    * Question Text: I understand the ramifications of not including the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission in the manifest file when targeting Android 13 and would like to turn off release errors.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"id\":\"c3\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"},{\"content\":\"### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED\\\", \\\"booleanResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": true } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LIST\\\", \\\"groupResponse\\\": { \\\"groups\\\": [ { \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NAME\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"Test Account 1\\\" } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"testuser1\\\" } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"password123\\\" } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\\", \\\"multipleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"values\\\": [ \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\\" ] } } ] } ] } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\\", \\\"multipleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"values\\\": [ \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\\" ] } } ] }\\n\\n## 6. Privacy Policy Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\\n\\n    * Type: String\\n    * Question Text: Add a privacy policy to the store listing to help provide transparency about how sensitive user and device data is treated.\\n[Learn more](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/9859455#privacy_policy). A privacy policy must be added if the app's target audience includes children under 13. Check the\\n[User Data policy](https://play.google.com/about/privacy-and-security.html)to avoid common violations.\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"https://www.example.com/privacy\\\" } } ] }\",\"id\":\"c9\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"},{\"content\":\"## 7. Target Audience & Content (TAC) Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_TARGET_AGE_GROUPS\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: What are the target age groups of the app?\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * 5 and under ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_FIVE_AND_UNDER )\\n        * 6-8 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIX_TO_EIGHT )\\n        * 9-12 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_NINE_TO_TWELVE )\\n        * 13-15 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_THIRTEEN_TO_FIFTEEN )\\n        * 16-17 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIXTEEN_AND_SEVENTEEN )\\n        * 18 and over ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE )\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Always required. A consecutive set of age bands must be selected.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_RESTRICT_MINOR_ACCESS\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: Restrict users that Google has determined to be minors from the app (optional)\\n    * Helper Text: The developer confirms that Google Play should block users determined to be minors from: Searching for or downloading the app on Google Play; Making in-app purchases, including new subscription sign ups, and renewals for existing subscribers. I acknowledge that Google Play may not be able to block all minor users who have not declared themselves to be under the age of 18.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_RESTRICT_MINOR_ACCESS\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Shown if only POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE is selected.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_COMPLIES_WITH_CHILDREN_LAWS_CERTIFICATION\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: The developer certifies that the app (including all APIs, SDKs, and ads) complies with all applicable laws and regulations relating to children. Examples include the US Children's Online Privacy Protection Act COPPA, and the EU General Data Protection Regulation GDPR.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_CHILDREN_LAWS_CERTIFIED\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_ADS_FROM_GOOGLE_PLAY_CERTIFIED_AD_NETWORKS\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: The developer certifies that all ads in the app are from Google Play certified ad networks and are suitable for all audiences, including families and children.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_ADS_FROM_GOOGLE_PLAY_CERTIFIED_AD_NETWORKS\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected AND the app has declared it contains ads in the\\n[Ads Declaration](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations#ads-declaration).\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_JOIN_TEACHER_APPROVED_PROGRAM\\n\\n    * Type: Single Choice\\n    * Question Text: Join the Teacher Approved program\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * Include the app in the Teacher Approved program ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_INCLUDE_IN_TEACHER_APPROVED )\\n        * Do not include the app in the Teacher Approved program ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_DO_NOT_INCLUDE_IN_TEACHER_APPROVED )\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_TARGET_AGE_GROUPS\\\", \\\"multipleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"values\\\": [ \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_THIRTEEN_TO_FIFTEEN\\\", \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIXTEEN_AND_SEVENTEEN\\\", \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE\\\" ] } } ] }\\n\\n## 8. Ads Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADS_DECLARATION\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_ADS_CONTAINS_ADS\\n\\n    * Type: Single Choice\\n    * Question Text: Does the app contain ads? Check the\\n[Ads policy](https://play.google.com/about/monetization-ads/ads/)to make sure the app is compliant.\\n    * Allowed Responses:\\n\\n        * Yes, the app contains ads ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_HAS_ADS )\\n        * No, the app does not contain ads ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_NO_ADS )\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADS_DECLARATION\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_ADS_CONTAINS_ADS\\\", \\\"singleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_HAS_ADS\\\" } } ] }\",\"id\":\"c10\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"},{\"content\":\"## 5. Testing Credentials Declaration (Sign in details)\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED\\n\\n    * Type: Boolean\\n    * Question Text: Is any part of the app restricted?\\n    * Helper Text:\\n\\n        * Yes: If the app includes any of the following: account sign in details, such as an email address, username, Google Account sign in, and / or SSO; payments, such as one-time products, memberships, subscriptions, and / or access tiers; referral codes and / or QR codes; one-time PINs and / or 2-step verification; biometric authentication; actions to be carried out on another device.\\n        * No: If any of the following apply to the app: no part of the app is restricted; no account sign in required in any country / region; no account sign in required and no content requires payment.\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LIST\\n\\n    * Type: Repeating Group (Max 5 sets of credentials)\\n    * Question Text: Sign in details\\n    * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED is true.\\n    * Nested Questions:\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NAME\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Name\\n            * Helper Text: Name this set of sign in details so that we can recognize what they're for. For example, 'Admin account' or 'User account'.\\n            * Conditions: Always required within the group.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Username, email address, or phone number\\n            * Helper Text: For phone numbers, include the country code and area code.\\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS are empty.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Password\\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS are empty.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Any other information required to access the app\\n            * Helper Text: Provide any other information required to access the app. If the app only requires a username and password, provide these using the preceding fields. Examples of restricted access other than a username and password include, but aren't limited to: 2-step verification, QR codes, location-based access, memberships, biometric logins...\\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD are empty.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\n\\n            * Type: Multiple Choice\\n            * Question Text: Sign in details in this declaration provide full access to all the features and content within this app, including premium or paid content.\\n            * Choices:\\n\\n                * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\n\\n\\n            * Conditions: Always required within the group.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: Allow Android to use the provided sign in details for performance and app compatibility testing. Tests are used to improve app compatibility with different Android devices and versions.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Shown if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED is true.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"id\":\"c8\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"}]}"}]},"uuid":"0339b60e-5d3f-4428-8be5-7b4392563749","timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:55:10.596Z","toolUseResult":"{\"results\":[{\"content\":\"### Policy Declarations\\n\\nWhen submitting or updating app information using the API, you must include any required policy declarations.Declaration RequirementsThe following declarations are in scope: Required for all apps to confirm if additional declarations are needed:\\n\\n* Health Apps: Tell us what health features the app uses to help us to understand which requirements the app must meet in the Health apps policy.\\n* Financial Features: Apps that provide financial features might need to comply with certain regulations in some countries or regions. Submit accurate and up-to-date details of the financial features in the app to help us make sure the right teams review the submission.\\n* Advertising ID: Help us understand whether the app uses advertising ID.\\n* Testing Credentials (Sign in details): If any part of the app is restricted based on sign in details, memberships, location, or other forms of authentication, provide instructions on how to access them.\\n* Privacy Policy: A link to and details about the app's privacy policy.\\n* Target Audience and Content: You must let us know the target age group of the app, and other information about its contents. This helps make sure that apps designed for children are safe and appropriate.\\n* Ads: You must let us know whether the app contains ads.\\n\\nConditionally Required:\\n\\n* Government Apps: Tell us if the app is for use by a government of any kind. This includes national, state and city governments, and local authorities. This helps us to make sure the right teams review the submission. If this declaration is not completed, the app will be considered not a government app.\\n* Child Safety Standards: Required for apps in the \\\"Social\\\" or \\\"Dating\\\" categories. Apps in the social or dating categories must provide published safety standards and contact information to comply with our\\n[child safety standards policy](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/14747720).\\n* News and Magazine Apps: Required for apps in the \\\"News and Magazines\\\" category. Add details about the news and magazine app to provide transparency about the entities behind the app.\\n\\nNote: Refer to the\\n[detailed guide](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations)to get a complete overview of each declaration, including question IDs, choice IDs, and examples.API Request StructurePolicy declarations are provided within the policyDeclarations array in the body of the\\n[UpdateAppStoreHostedAppRequest](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/api-ref/rest/v3/appstoreappsreview/updateappstorehostedapp). Each item in this array is an AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration object. AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration Object:\\n\\n* declarationId (string, Required): The unique identifier for the policy declaration (e.g., POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_FINANCE , POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT ).\\n* responses (Array of PolicyResponse , Required): A list of answers to the questions within that specific declaration.\\n\\nPolicyResponse Object:\",\"id\":\"c3\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review\"},{\"content\":\"## 2. Advertising ID Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADVERTISING_ID\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_IS_USED\\n\\n    * Type: Boolean\\n    * Question Text: Does the app use advertising ID? This includes any SDKs that the app imports that use advertising ID.\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_PURPOSE\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: Why does the app need to use advertising ID? This includes any SDKs the app imports that use advertising IDs. When this question is answered, make sure to verify if any third-party SDK code in the app uses advertising ID. If so, it must be declared that the app uses it. Some SDKs, such as the Google Mobile Ads SDK (Play Services-ads) may already declare the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission in the SDK's library manifest. If the app uses these SDKs as dependencies, the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission from the SDK's library manifest will be merged with the app's main manifest by default, even if the permission is not explicitly declared.\\n[Learn more](https://developer.android.com/studio/build/manage-manifests#merge-manifests).\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * App functionality ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_APP_FUNCTIONALITY )\\n\\n            * Used for features in the app. For example, to enable functionality, or authenticate users.\\n\\n\\n        * Analytics ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ANALYTICS )\\n\\n            * Used to collect data about how users use the app, or how the app performs. For example, to see how many users are using a particular feature, to monitor app health, to diagnose and fix bugs or crashes, or to make future performance improvements.\\n\\n\\n        * Developer communications ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_DEVELOPER_COMMUNICATIONS )\\n\\n            * Used to send news or notifications about the developer or the app. For example, sending a push notification to inform users about an important security update, or informing users about new features in the app.\\n\\n\\n        * Fraud prevention, security, and compliance ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_FRAUD_PREVENTION_SECURITY )\\n\\n            * Used for fraud prevention, security, or compliance with laws. For example, monitoring failed login attempts to identify possible fraudulent activity.\\n\\n\\n        * Advertising or marketing ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ADVERTISING )\\n\\n            * Used to display or target ads or marketing communications, or measure ad performance. For example, displaying ads in the app, sending push notifications to promote other products or services, or sharing data with advertising partners.\\n\\n\\n        * Personalization ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_PERSONALIZATION )\\n\\n            * Used to customize the app, such as showing recommended content or suggestions. For example, suggesting playlists based on users' listening habits, or delivering local news based on a user's location.\\n\\n\\n        * Account management ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT )\\n\\n            * Used for the setup or management of user accounts. For example, to enable users to create accounts; to add information to accounts provided for use across services; to log in to the app; or to verify their credentials.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_IS_USED is true.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_ACK\\n\\n    * Type: Boolean\\n    * Question Text: I understand the ramifications of not including the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission in the manifest file when targeting Android 13 and would like to turn off release errors.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"id\":\"c3\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"},{\"content\":\"### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED\\\", \\\"booleanResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": true } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LIST\\\", \\\"groupResponse\\\": { \\\"groups\\\": [ { \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NAME\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"Test Account 1\\\" } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"testuser1\\\" } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"password123\\\" } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\\", \\\"multipleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"values\\\": [ \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\\" ] } } ] } ] } }, { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\\", \\\"multipleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"values\\\": [ \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\\" ] } } ] }\\n\\n## 6. Privacy Policy Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\\n\\n    * Type: String\\n    * Question Text: Add a privacy policy to the store listing to help provide transparency about how sensitive user and device data is treated.\\n[Learn more](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/9859455#privacy_policy). A privacy policy must be added if the app's target audience includes children under 13. Check the\\n[User Data policy](https://play.google.com/about/privacy-and-security.html)to avoid common violations.\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\\\", \\\"stringResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"https://www.example.com/privacy\\\" } } ] }\",\"id\":\"c9\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"},{\"content\":\"## 7. Target Audience & Content (TAC) Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_TARGET_AGE_GROUPS\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: What are the target age groups of the app?\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * 5 and under ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_FIVE_AND_UNDER )\\n        * 6-8 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIX_TO_EIGHT )\\n        * 9-12 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_NINE_TO_TWELVE )\\n        * 13-15 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_THIRTEEN_TO_FIFTEEN )\\n        * 16-17 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIXTEEN_AND_SEVENTEEN )\\n        * 18 and over ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE )\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Always required. A consecutive set of age bands must be selected.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_RESTRICT_MINOR_ACCESS\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: Restrict users that Google has determined to be minors from the app (optional)\\n    * Helper Text: The developer confirms that Google Play should block users determined to be minors from: Searching for or downloading the app on Google Play; Making in-app purchases, including new subscription sign ups, and renewals for existing subscribers. I acknowledge that Google Play may not be able to block all minor users who have not declared themselves to be under the age of 18.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_RESTRICT_MINOR_ACCESS\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Shown if only POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE is selected.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_COMPLIES_WITH_CHILDREN_LAWS_CERTIFICATION\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: The developer certifies that the app (including all APIs, SDKs, and ads) complies with all applicable laws and regulations relating to children. Examples include the US Children's Online Privacy Protection Act COPPA, and the EU General Data Protection Regulation GDPR.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_CHILDREN_LAWS_CERTIFIED\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_ADS_FROM_GOOGLE_PLAY_CERTIFIED_AD_NETWORKS\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: The developer certifies that all ads in the app are from Google Play certified ad networks and are suitable for all audiences, including families and children.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_ADS_FROM_GOOGLE_PLAY_CERTIFIED_AD_NETWORKS\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected AND the app has declared it contains ads in the\\n[Ads Declaration](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations#ads-declaration).\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_JOIN_TEACHER_APPROVED_PROGRAM\\n\\n    * Type: Single Choice\\n    * Question Text: Join the Teacher Approved program\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * Include the app in the Teacher Approved program ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_INCLUDE_IN_TEACHER_APPROVED )\\n        * Do not include the app in the Teacher Approved program ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_DO_NOT_INCLUDE_IN_TEACHER_APPROVED )\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_TARGET_AGE_GROUPS\\\", \\\"multipleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"values\\\": [ \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_THIRTEEN_TO_FIFTEEN\\\", \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIXTEEN_AND_SEVENTEEN\\\", \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE\\\" ] } } ] }\\n\\n## 8. Ads Declaration\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADS_DECLARATION\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_ADS_CONTAINS_ADS\\n\\n    * Type: Single Choice\\n    * Question Text: Does the app contain ads? Check the\\n[Ads policy](https://play.google.com/about/monetization-ads/ads/)to make sure the app is compliant.\\n    * Allowed Responses:\\n\\n        * Yes, the app contains ads ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_HAS_ADS )\\n        * No, the app does not contain ads ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_NO_ADS )\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Example JSON\\n\\n{ \\\"declarationId\\\": \\\"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADS_DECLARATION\\\", \\\"responses\\\": [ { \\\"questionId\\\": \\\"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_ADS_CONTAINS_ADS\\\", \\\"singleChoiceResponse\\\": { \\\"value\\\": \\\"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_HAS_ADS\\\" } } ] }\",\"id\":\"c10\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"},{\"content\":\"## 5. Testing Credentials Declaration (Sign in details)\\n\\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED\\n\\n    * Type: Boolean\\n    * Question Text: Is any part of the app restricted?\\n    * Helper Text:\\n\\n        * Yes: If the app includes any of the following: account sign in details, such as an email address, username, Google Account sign in, and / or SSO; payments, such as one-time products, memberships, subscriptions, and / or access tiers; referral codes and / or QR codes; one-time PINs and / or 2-step verification; biometric authentication; actions to be carried out on another device.\\n        * No: If any of the following apply to the app: no part of the app is restricted; no account sign in required in any country / region; no account sign in required and no content requires payment.\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Always required.\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LIST\\n\\n    * Type: Repeating Group (Max 5 sets of credentials)\\n    * Question Text: Sign in details\\n    * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED is true.\\n    * Nested Questions:\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NAME\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Name\\n            * Helper Text: Name this set of sign in details so that we can recognize what they're for. For example, 'Admin account' or 'User account'.\\n            * Conditions: Always required within the group.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Username, email address, or phone number\\n            * Helper Text: For phone numbers, include the country code and area code.\\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS are empty.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Password\\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS are empty.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS\\n\\n            * Type: String\\n            * Question Text: Any other information required to access the app\\n            * Helper Text: Provide any other information required to access the app. If the app only requires a username and password, provide these using the preceding fields. Examples of restricted access other than a username and password include, but aren't limited to: 2-step verification, QR codes, location-based access, memberships, biometric logins...\\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD are empty.\\n\\n\\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\n\\n            * Type: Multiple Choice\\n            * Question Text: Sign in details in this declaration provide full access to all the features and content within this app, including premium or paid content.\\n            * Choices:\\n\\n                * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\\n\\n\\n            * Conditions: Always required within the group.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\n\\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\\n    * Question Text: Allow Android to use the provided sign in details for performance and app compatibility testing. Tests are used to improve app compatibility with different Android devices and versions.\\n    * Choices:\\n\\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\\n\\n\\n    * Conditions: Shown if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED is true.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"id\":\"c8\",\"parent\":\"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations\"}]}","mcpMeta":{"structuredContent":{"results":[{"content":"### Policy Declarations\n\nWhen submitting or updating app information using the API, you must include any required policy declarations.Declaration RequirementsThe following declarations are in scope: Required for all apps to confirm if additional declarations are needed:\n\n* Health Apps: Tell us what health features the app uses to help us to understand which requirements the app must meet in the Health apps policy.\n* Financial Features: Apps that provide financial features might need to comply with certain regulations in some countries or regions. Submit accurate and up-to-date details of the financial features in the app to help us make sure the right teams review the submission.\n* Advertising ID: Help us understand whether the app uses advertising ID.\n* Testing Credentials (Sign in details): If any part of the app is restricted based on sign in details, memberships, location, or other forms of authentication, provide instructions on how to access them.\n* Privacy Policy: A link to and details about the app's privacy policy.\n* Target Audience and Content: You must let us know the target age group of the app, and other information about its contents. This helps make sure that apps designed for children are safe and appropriate.\n* Ads: You must let us know whether the app contains ads.\n\nConditionally Required:\n\n* Government Apps: Tell us if the app is for use by a government of any kind. This includes national, state and city governments, and local authorities. This helps us to make sure the right teams review the submission. If this declaration is not completed, the app will be considered not a government app.\n* Child Safety Standards: Required for apps in the \"Social\" or \"Dating\" categories. Apps in the social or dating categories must provide published safety standards and contact information to comply with our\n[child safety standards policy](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/14747720).\n* News and Magazine Apps: Required for apps in the \"News and Magazines\" category. Add details about the news and magazine app to provide transparency about the entities behind the app.\n\nNote: Refer to the\n[detailed guide](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations)to get a complete overview of each declaration, including question IDs, choice IDs, and examples.API Request StructurePolicy declarations are provided within the policyDeclarations array in the body of the\n[UpdateAppStoreHostedAppRequest](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/api-ref/rest/v3/appstoreappsreview/updateappstorehostedapp). Each item in this array is an AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration object. AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration Object:\n\n* declarationId (string, Required): The unique identifier for the policy declaration (e.g., POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_FINANCE , POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT ).\n* responses (Array of PolicyResponse , Required): A list of answers to the questions within that specific declaration.\n\nPolicyResponse Object:","id":"c3","parent":"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review"},{"content":"## 2. Advertising ID Declaration\n\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADVERTISING_ID\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_IS_USED\n\n    * Type: Boolean\n    * Question Text: Does the app use advertising ID? This includes any SDKs that the app imports that use advertising ID.\n    * Conditions: Always required.\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_PURPOSE\n\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\n    * Question Text: Why does the app need to use advertising ID? This includes any SDKs the app imports that use advertising IDs. When this question is answered, make sure to verify if any third-party SDK code in the app uses advertising ID. If so, it must be declared that the app uses it. Some SDKs, such as the Google Mobile Ads SDK (Play Services-ads) may already declare the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission in the SDK's library manifest. If the app uses these SDKs as dependencies, the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission from the SDK's library manifest will be merged with the app's main manifest by default, even if the permission is not explicitly declared.\n[Learn more](https://developer.android.com/studio/build/manage-manifests#merge-manifests).\n    * Choices:\n\n        * App functionality ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_APP_FUNCTIONALITY )\n\n            * Used for features in the app. For example, to enable functionality, or authenticate users.\n\n\n        * Analytics ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ANALYTICS )\n\n            * Used to collect data about how users use the app, or how the app performs. For example, to see how many users are using a particular feature, to monitor app health, to diagnose and fix bugs or crashes, or to make future performance improvements.\n\n\n        * Developer communications ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_DEVELOPER_COMMUNICATIONS )\n\n            * Used to send news or notifications about the developer or the app. For example, sending a push notification to inform users about an important security update, or informing users about new features in the app.\n\n\n        * Fraud prevention, security, and compliance ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_FRAUD_PREVENTION_SECURITY )\n\n            * Used for fraud prevention, security, or compliance with laws. For example, monitoring failed login attempts to identify possible fraudulent activity.\n\n\n        * Advertising or marketing ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ADVERTISING )\n\n            * Used to display or target ads or marketing communications, or measure ad performance. For example, displaying ads in the app, sending push notifications to promote other products or services, or sharing data with advertising partners.\n\n\n        * Personalization ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_PERSONALIZATION )\n\n            * Used to customize the app, such as showing recommended content or suggestions. For example, suggesting playlists based on users' listening habits, or delivering local news based on a user's location.\n\n\n        * Account management ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_PSL_ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT )\n\n            * Used for the setup or management of user accounts. For example, to enable users to create accounts; to add information to accounts provided for use across services; to log in to the app; or to verify their credentials.\n\n\n\n\n    * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_IS_USED is true.\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_AD_ID_ACK\n\n    * Type: Boolean\n    * Question Text: I understand the ramifications of not including the com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID permission in the manifest file when targeting Android 13 and would like to turn off release errors.\n\n\n\n","id":"c3","parent":"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations"},{"content":"### Example JSON\n\n{ \"declarationId\": \"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS\", \"responses\": [ { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED\", \"booleanResponse\": { \"value\": true } }, { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LIST\", \"groupResponse\": { \"groups\": [ { \"responses\": [ { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NAME\", \"stringResponse\": { \"value\": \"Test Account 1\" } }, { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME\", \"stringResponse\": { \"value\": \"testuser1\" } }, { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD\", \"stringResponse\": { \"value\": \"password123\" } }, { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\", \"multipleChoiceResponse\": { \"values\": [ \"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\" ] } } ] } ] } }, { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\", \"multipleChoiceResponse\": { \"values\": [ \"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\" ] } } ] }\n\n## 6. Privacy Policy Declaration\n\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\n\n    * Type: String\n    * Question Text: Add a privacy policy to the store listing to help provide transparency about how sensitive user and device data is treated.\n[Learn more](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/9859455#privacy_policy). A privacy policy must be added if the app's target audience includes children under 13. Check the\n[User Data policy](https://play.google.com/about/privacy-and-security.html)to avoid common violations.\n    * Conditions: Always required.\n\n\n\n\n### Example JSON\n\n{ \"declarationId\": \"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY\", \"responses\": [ { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\", \"stringResponse\": { \"value\": \"https://www.example.com/privacy\" } } ] }","id":"c9","parent":"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations"},{"content":"## 7. Target Audience & Content (TAC) Declaration\n\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_TARGET_AGE_GROUPS\n\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\n    * Question Text: What are the target age groups of the app?\n    * Choices:\n\n        * 5 and under ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_FIVE_AND_UNDER )\n        * 6-8 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIX_TO_EIGHT )\n        * 9-12 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_NINE_TO_TWELVE )\n        * 13-15 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_THIRTEEN_TO_FIFTEEN )\n        * 16-17 ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIXTEEN_AND_SEVENTEEN )\n        * 18 and over ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE )\n\n\n    * Conditions: Always required. A consecutive set of age bands must be selected.\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_RESTRICT_MINOR_ACCESS\n\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\n    * Question Text: Restrict users that Google has determined to be minors from the app (optional)\n    * Helper Text: The developer confirms that Google Play should block users determined to be minors from: Searching for or downloading the app on Google Play; Making in-app purchases, including new subscription sign ups, and renewals for existing subscribers. I acknowledge that Google Play may not be able to block all minor users who have not declared themselves to be under the age of 18.\n    * Choices:\n\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_RESTRICT_MINOR_ACCESS\n\n\n    * Conditions: Shown if only POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE is selected.\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_COMPLIES_WITH_CHILDREN_LAWS_CERTIFICATION\n\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\n    * Question Text: The developer certifies that the app (including all APIs, SDKs, and ads) complies with all applicable laws and regulations relating to children. Examples include the US Children's Online Privacy Protection Act COPPA, and the EU General Data Protection Regulation GDPR.\n    * Choices:\n\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_CHILDREN_LAWS_CERTIFIED\n\n\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected.\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_ADS_FROM_GOOGLE_PLAY_CERTIFIED_AD_NETWORKS\n\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\n    * Question Text: The developer certifies that all ads in the app are from Google Play certified ad networks and are suitable for all audiences, including families and children.\n    * Choices:\n\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_ADS_FROM_GOOGLE_PLAY_CERTIFIED_AD_NETWORKS\n\n\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected AND the app has declared it contains ads in the\n[Ads Declaration](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations#ads-declaration).\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_JOIN_TEACHER_APPROVED_PROGRAM\n\n    * Type: Single Choice\n    * Question Text: Join the Teacher Approved program\n    * Choices:\n\n        * Include the app in the Teacher Approved program ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_INCLUDE_IN_TEACHER_APPROVED )\n        * Do not include the app in the Teacher Approved program ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_DO_NOT_INCLUDE_IN_TEACHER_APPROVED )\n\n\n    * Conditions: Required if any age group 12 and under is selected.\n\n\n\n\n### Example JSON\n\n{ \"declarationId\": \"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TARGET_AUDIENCE_CONTENT\", \"responses\": [ { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TAC_TARGET_AGE_GROUPS\", \"multipleChoiceResponse\": { \"values\": [ \"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_THIRTEEN_TO_FIFTEEN\", \"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_SIXTEEN_AND_SEVENTEEN\", \"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TAC_AGE_EIGHTEEN_AND_ABOVE\" ] } } ] }\n\n## 8. Ads Declaration\n\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADS_DECLARATION\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_ADS_CONTAINS_ADS\n\n    * Type: Single Choice\n    * Question Text: Does the app contain ads? Check the\n[Ads policy](https://play.google.com/about/monetization-ads/ads/)to make sure the app is compliant.\n    * Allowed Responses:\n\n        * Yes, the app contains ads ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_HAS_ADS )\n        * No, the app does not contain ads ( POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_NO_ADS )\n\n\n    * Conditions: Always required.\n\n\n\n\n### Example JSON\n\n{ \"declarationId\": \"POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_ADS_DECLARATION\", \"responses\": [ { \"questionId\": \"POLICY_QUESTION_ID_ADS_CONTAINS_ADS\", \"singleChoiceResponse\": { \"value\": \"POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_ADS_HAS_ADS\" } } ] }","id":"c10","parent":"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations"},{"content":"## 5. Testing Credentials Declaration (Sign in details)\n\nDeclaration ID: POLICY_DECLARATION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED\n\n    * Type: Boolean\n    * Question Text: Is any part of the app restricted?\n    * Helper Text:\n\n        * Yes: If the app includes any of the following: account sign in details, such as an email address, username, Google Account sign in, and / or SSO; payments, such as one-time products, memberships, subscriptions, and / or access tiers; referral codes and / or QR codes; one-time PINs and / or 2-step verification; biometric authentication; actions to be carried out on another device.\n        * No: If any of the following apply to the app: no part of the app is restricted; no account sign in required in any country / region; no account sign in required and no content requires payment.\n\n\n    * Conditions: Always required.\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LIST\n\n    * Type: Repeating Group (Max 5 sets of credentials)\n    * Question Text: Sign in details\n    * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED is true.\n    * Nested Questions:\n\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NAME\n\n            * Type: String\n            * Question Text: Name\n            * Helper Text: Name this set of sign in details so that we can recognize what they're for. For example, 'Admin account' or 'User account'.\n            * Conditions: Always required within the group.\n\n\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME\n\n            * Type: String\n            * Question Text: Username, email address, or phone number\n            * Helper Text: For phone numbers, include the country code and area code.\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS are empty.\n\n\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD\n\n            * Type: String\n            * Question Text: Password\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS are empty.\n\n\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS\n\n            * Type: String\n            * Question Text: Any other information required to access the app\n            * Helper Text: Provide any other information required to access the app. If the app only requires a username and password, provide these using the preceding fields. Examples of restricted access other than a username and password include, but aren't limited to: 2-step verification, QR codes, location-based access, memberships, biometric logins...\n            * Conditions: Required if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_USERNAME AND POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_PASSWORD are empty.\n\n\n        * Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\n\n            * Type: Multiple Choice\n            * Question Text: Sign in details in this declaration provide full access to all the features and content within this app, including premium or paid content.\n            * Choices:\n\n                * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_NO_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_REQUIRED\n\n\n            * Conditions: Always required within the group.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n* Question ID: POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\n\n    * Type: Multiple Choice\n    * Question Text: Allow Android to use the provided sign in details for performance and app compatibility testing. Tests are used to improve app compatibility with different Android devices and versions.\n    * Choices:\n\n        * POLICY_RESPONSE_CHOICE_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_ANDROID_TESTING_CONSENT\n\n\n    * Conditions: Shown if POLICY_QUESTION_ID_TESTING_CREDENTIALS_LOGIN_REQUIRED is true.\n\n\n\n","id":"c8","parent":"documents/developers.google.com/android-publisher/app-store-review/policy-declarations"}]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62430775-ce5d-483b-ba51-ff7439d843d5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\mp-sweep-404-sdk-headers","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
