{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","hash":"e9a583919f7fce6541653e9961669e0d5ac92b6dad9351d042a86759285d658d","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VZCsBfSZ5atdr8iqetUPRm","type":"tool_result","content":"linhas: 332\r\ntotal de métodos: 145\r\nmétodos com 'rating': \r\nmétodos com 'categor': \r\nmétodos com 'audience': \r\nmétodos com 'safety': androidpublisher.applications.dataSafety  POST androidpublisher/v3/applications/{packageName}/dataSafety\r\nmétodos com 'iarc': \r\nmétodos com 'questionnaire': \r\nmétodos com 'policy': androidpublisher.appstoreappsreview.uploadappstoreapppolicydeclarationfile  POST androidpublisher/v3/appstore/{appStorePackageName}/apps/{packageName}/policyDeclarationFiles:upload\r\nschemas com 'rating': RegionalProductAgeRatingInfo\r\nschemas com 'categor': \r\nschemas com 'audience': \r\nschemas com 'safety': SafetyLabelsUpdateResponse, SafetyLabelsUpdateRequest\r\nschemas com 'iarc': \r\nschemas com 'questionnaire': \r\nschemas com 'policy': UploadAppStoreAppPolicyDeclarationFileRequest, PolicyBooleanResponse, PolicySingleChoiceResponse, NestedPolicyResponse, PolicyGroupResponse, PolicyStringResponse, PolicyMultipleChoiceResponse, AppStoreAppPolicyDeclaration, PolicyKeyedGrou\r\nschema AppDetails (edits.details): contactPhone, contactWebsite, defaultLanguage, contactEmail\r\nschema Listing (edits.listings): video, language, title, fullDescription, shortDescription\r\nedits.details.get -> HTTP 200 | { \"defaultLanguage\": \"pt-BR\", \"contactWebsite\": \"https://www.lcv.dev\", \"contactEmail\": \"suporte@lcv.dev\", \"contactPhone\": \"+551152290077\" } \r\nedits.listings.list -> HTTP 200 | { \"kind\": \"androidpublisher#listingsListResponse\", \"listings\": [ { \"language\": \"pt-BR\", \"title\": \"Oráculo Celestial\", \"fullDescription\": \"Oráculo Celestial reúne, em um só aplicativo, o cálculo preciso do seu mapa de nasciment\r\nedits.tracks.list -> HTTP 200 | { \"kind\": \"androidpublisher#tracksListResponse\", \"tracks\": [ { \"track\": \"production\", \"releases\": [ { \"status\": \"draft\" } ] }, { \"track\": \"beta\", \"releases\": [ { \"name\": \"3 (0.3.0)\", \"versionCodes\": [ \"3\" ], \"status\": \"draft\" } \r\nedits.countryavailability.get(production) -> HTTP 200 | { \"countries\": [ { \"countryCode\": \"AE\" }, { \"countryCode\": \"AG\" }, { \"countryCode\": \"AL\" }, { \"countryCode\": \"AM\" }, { \"countryCode\": \"AO\" }, { \"countryCode\": \"AR\" }, { \"countryCode\": \"AT\" }, { \"countryCo\r\nedits.testers.get(internal) -> HTTP 200 | {} \r\ninappproducts.list -> HTTP 403 | Please migrate to the new publishing API.\r\nmonetization.onetimeproducts.list -> HTTP 404 | Falha na conversão de JSON com o erro: Unexpected character encountered while parsing value: E. Path '', line 5, position 2.\r\napplications.dataSafety (GET, método inexistente na doc) -> HTTP 404 | Falha na conversão de JSON com o erro: Unexpected character encountered while parsing value: E. Path '', line 5, position 2.\r\napplications.tracks.releases.list(production) -> HTTP 200 | { \"releases\": [ { \"releaseLifecycleState\": \"RELEASE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_DRAFT\", \"track\": \"production\" } ] } \r\nHIGH\t//artifactregistry.googleapis.com/projects/lcv-ideas-and-software/locations/us-central1/repositories/astrologo-paid-cmek/dockerImages/astrologo-paid-runner@sha256:69a2a1c4f0823abfa3fbb07eda5f5ac5cf3c998bee872e98e883e9aabffe944e\t2026-10-30T00:01:08.053Z\r\nHIGH\t//artifactregistry.googleapis.com/projects/lcv-ideas-and-software/locations/us-central1/repositories/astrologo-paid-cmek/dockerImages/astrologo-paid-runner@sha256:d6a12c54ea91bc4f787d775fa11f52715180b423784c674742ef8ac0716087b0\t2026-10-30T00:09:05.281Z\r\nHIGH\t//artifactregistry.googleapis.com/projects/lcv-ideas-and-software/locations/us-central1/repositories/astrologo-paid-cmek/dockerImages/astrologo-paid-runner@sha256:0b404cc2714e0ec281a8f770909c04ff2f7b033d6dd1baae2958d5e310612a3a\t2026-10-30T01:04:25.361Z\r\nHIGH\t//artifactregistry.googleapis.com/projects/lcv-ideas-and-software/locations/us-central1/repositories/astrologo-paid-cmek/dockerImages/astrologo-paid-runner@sha256:a45d7b3785d183311fa20f0b931d86b5faa3e6c4e02cc4efc9eea5674d6bce70\t2026-10-30T01:16:13.827Z\r\nERROR: (gcloud.artifacts.docker.images.describe) Image not found.\r\nERROR: (gcloud.artifacts.docker.images.describe) Image not found.\r\nERROR: (gcloud.artifacts.docker.images.describe) Image not found.\r\nERROR: (gcloud.artifacts.docker.images.describe) Image not found.\r\n      analysisStatus: FINISHED_SUCCESS\r\n      analysisStatus: FINISHED_SUCCESS\r\nfim 30/10/2026 01:59:37","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FfQSuoEqSSVq1YyE1anPsA","type":"tool_result","content":"          tag=$(printf 'v%02d.%02d.%02d' \"$major\" \"$minor\" \"$patch\")\n          echo \"name=$name\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          echo \"tag=$tag\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Refuse an existing production Release or tag\n        if: inputs.track == 'production' && inputs.release_status == 'completed'\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN }}\n          TAG: ${{ steps.version.outputs.tag }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          refs=$(gh api \"repos/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/git/matching-refs/tags/$TAG\")\n          count=$(jq -er --arg ref \"refs/tags/$TAG\" 'map(select(.ref == $ref)) | length' <<< \"$refs\")\n          if [ \"$count\" != 0 ]; then\n            echo \"::error::The production tag $TAG already exists; preserve it and use a new versionName.\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          releases=$(gh api --paginate --slurp \"repos/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/releases?per_page=100\")\n          if ! jq -e --arg tag \"$TAG\" 'all(.[][]; .tag_name != $tag)' <<< \"$releases\" >/dev/null; then\n            echo \"::error::A Release or draft already uses $TAG; do not upload this version again.\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n\n      - name: Build the release bundle\n        env:\n=== 360-392\n          echo \"version_code=$version\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      # Native evidence of a completed production edit, distinct from the\n      # generic upload/commit stage that also succeeds for nonpublic tracks.\n      - name: Confirm the committed production release\n        if: success() && inputs.track == 'production' && inputs.release_status == 'completed'\n        env:\n          VERSION_CODE: ${{ steps.play.outputs.version_code }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          if [ -z \"$VERSION_CODE\" ]; then\n            echo \"::error::The committed production edit has no versionCode.\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          echo \"- production/completed Play edit committed for versionCode \\`$VERSION_CODE\\`\" >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n\n      # This separate native step preserves the successful upload/commit result\n      # if Play processing or later Release recording fails. Never upload again\n      # to recover an already committed versionCode.\n      - name: Download the Play-signed universal APK\n        id: apk\n        env:\n          VERSION_NAME: ${{ steps.version.outputs.name }}\n          VERSION_CODE: ${{ steps.play.outputs.version_code }}\n          TOKEN: ${{ steps.auth.outputs.access_token }}\n          QUOTA_PROJECT: ${{ vars.GCP_QUOTA_PROJECT }}\n          PACKAGE: ${{ vars.PLAY_PACKAGE_NAME }}\n          TRACK: ${{ inputs.track }}\n          RELEASE_STATUS: ${{ inputs.release_status }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          play() {\n            local rotulo=$1; shift\n=== 440-470\n\n          # A committed production edit may still await review/manual publish.\n          # Read the native lifecycle; generated APKs alone do not prove this.\n          lifecycle=$(play \"consultar publicação efetiva\" \\\n            -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n            -H \"x-goog-user-project: $QUOTA_PROJECT\" \\\n            --connect-timeout 10 --max-time 120 \\\n            \"$api/$PACKAGE/tracks/production/releases\")\n          if ! printf '%s' \"$lifecycle\" | jq -e --argjson code \"$version\" '\n            type == \"object\" and (.releases | type == \"array\") and\n            any(.releases[];\n              .track == \"production\" and\n              .releaseLifecycleState == \"RELEASE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_PUBLISHED\" and\n              (.activeArtifacts | type == \"array\") and\n              any(.activeArtifacts[];\n                (.versionCode | type == \"number\" and floor == .) and\n                .versionCode == $code\n              )\n            )\n          ' >/dev/null; then\n            echo \"- Production publication is not established by the native lifecycle/active artifact proof; no GitHub Release was recorded. After Google publishes this version, use record-play-release without re-uploading it.\" >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n            echo \"released=false\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n            exit 0\n          fi\n\n          # Production only: fetch the universal APK Google Play generated and\n          # signed with the app signing key. Play processes the bundle\n          # asynchronously and answers 404 or 409 until it is done, so poll.\n          # Ten minutes is far beyond the usual seconds; exceeding it is an\n          # error worth a human's eyes, not a reason to publish a Release\n          # without its artifact.\n=== README 534-560\n  recorded in `THIRDPARTY.md`), the security contact, the account-deletion page\n  and the Digital Asset Links statement in `site/.well-known/assetlinks.json`.\n- `publish-play.yml`, dispatched manually, builds the release App Bundle, sends\n  it to the chosen Google Play track and refuses to publish when the digest Play\n  received is not the artifact the job built. Its native edit commit uses\n  `ERROR_IF_IN_REVIEW`, preserving an existing Google review by refusing a new\n  submission until that review finishes. The release notes travel with it,\n  from `play/release-notes/pt-BR.txt`, because the API takes them in the track\n  update and a publication without them reaches the store with an empty \"what's\n  new\". A `release_status` input carries `completed` or `draft`: an app that has\n  never been published only accepts `draft` on the public track, and that first\n  publication is finished in the Play Console. A production publication also\n  records a GitHub Release with tag `vXX.XX.XX`, carrying the universal APK that\n  Google Play generated and signed with the app signing key — the same binary the\n  Play uses — plus `SHA256SUMS` and a provenance attestation. Both entrypoints\n  require the read-only production releases API to report `PUBLISHED` with the\n  exact source versionCode in `activeArtifacts` before downloading/recording.\n  A completed edit alone is not publication: the producer records no GitHub\n  Release while Google review/manual publication remains pending, preserving\n  its committed version for later recording. The native `PUBLISHED` lifecycle\n  also includes halted/resumable releases; Google controls current rollout and\n  availability, which these notes do not independently guarantee. Production\n  recording requires `PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN` before Google authentication, rejects\n  existing tags/drafts before upload, and atomically creates the tag at this\n  publishing run's exact source SHA. Native tag readbacks precede asset upload\n  and publication. Both Play entrypoints share this repository's `play-release`\n  concurrency group with native `queue: max`: up to 100 pending operations are","is_error":false},{"type":"text","text":"The user sent a new message while you were working:\ngh/LCV-Ideas-Software/-/trails/223/changes/astrologo-android/16 com finding.\n\nThis is how Claude Code surfaces messages the user sends mid-turn — within the running turn, often alongside the next tool result, rather than as a separate conversation turn. Address the message above as you continue this turn.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"The user sent a new message while you were working:\nCorrigir.\n\nThis is how Claude Code surfaces messages the user sends mid-turn — within the running turn, often alongside the next tool result, rather than as a separate conversation turn. Address the message above as you continue this turn."},{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","media_type":"image/png","data":""}}]}}
