{"parentUuid":"537f4021-6007-42be-81f0-411b7c33274d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ec5dd05e-bec6-412b-a2bc-8a4c30296990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Goal check-in: «Any claims or assertions you make must be thoroughly and irrefutably proven or demonstrated! I require concrete, irrefutable evidence for anything you label as \"pending\" or \"inconclusive.\" Always use the date and time formats standard in Brazil. Your internal communication should always take place in your native language, but when communicating with the operator, the use of Brazilian Portuguese is mandatory. It is strictly forbidden to infer, presume, guess, hallucinate, fabricate, or make decisions on one’s own. In the absence of data or information, it is mandatory to actively consult official documentation, forums, communities, or the Internet Archive. If it is not possible to resolve a question using these resources, the operator must be consulted. The redundancy of procedures is strictly prohibited, absent conclusive proof that such redundancy is absolutely necessary. The `D:` drive no longer exists. Save any materials that would otherwise be stored in `audits\\`, `deliverables\\`, or `Outros-Trabalhos\\` into a `temp\\` directory within each repository you are working on. Once the task is complete, delete this `temp\\` folder entirely, ensuring that everything which needs to be—or can be—saved is uploaded to GitHub or Linear. Repository branches/worktrees must be created exclusively within `C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\`. We follow a \"zero local retention\" policy: save everything that needs to be saved to Linear/GitHub, then delete it from your local machine. Assets, images, and designs may be kept in Figma or Canva, provided they are properly referenced and linked for easy retrieval. All API credentials, keys and tokens are stored in 1Password. Open a single, persistent, hidden terminal session using `op run` and execute all commands that rely on these credentials, keys and tokens within that session. Dedicate your full effort to \"deep research\" when seeking solutions to any problems encountered. Conduct an exhaustive, broad, and comprehensive investigation—consulting official documentation, forums, online communities, and the wider internet—before declaring any item as \"pending\" or a \"blocker.\" Before asking the operator for information you believe is missing, check existing records, chat logs, open/closed issues, etc. Always prioritize the use of native, official solutions—whether from GitHub, Google, or Android (as applicable)—as well as those from approved, official third-party providers. Any resources required for the correct and fully functional implementation of these native, official, and approved solutions must be provided. As a general rule, the use of custom modifications is prohibited. This policy may be relaxed on a case-by-case basis, subject to prior evaluation and approval by the operator. The use of central controllers is prohibited. Each repository functions as an independent, self-contained unit. While all repositories must adhere to established Enterprise/Organization guidelines, standards, and structures, they remain independent and isolated from one another. Utilize \"ultrabrain\" (collective/expert-level problem-solving), cross-reviews (reserved for complex cases that warrant such an approach), and official documentation. You are required to use native solutions and APIs from GitHub, Google, or Android (as applicable), or those from third-party providers approved by these platforms. Custom solutions should be used only as a last resort. Within the scope of this work, ensure that all GitHub Projects, Discussions, and Issues—as well as Linear’s Issues, Projects, Teams, Initiatives, Cycles, and Milestones, and Entire’s Trails, Dispatches, Checkouts, and Memorys—are kept up to date, linked, cross-referenced, and synchronized. This includes ensuring the accuracy of statuses, priorities, assignees, labels, and content across all items whenever updates, links, cross-references, or synchronization are required.» is still active, and evaluation has been deferred for 62 min because background work is still running:\n- bauxjpzhg · shell · python -X utf8 -I tools/op-terminal/opx.py --terminal default --timeout 2400 --shell pwsh --cwd C:… [+83 chars]\nCheck on their progress (e.g. read their output). If they are progressing, say so briefly and keep waiting; if they are stuck or no longer needed, fix or stop them and continue toward the goal."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"ee705cbe-9e3e-4b47-9612-af81bc5b5121","timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:47:38.620Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\github-operations","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
