{"parentUuid":"ee705cbe-9e3e-4b47-9612-af81bc5b5121","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-mythos-5-1","id":"msg_011CgXyRd92zgSnvzbFPwxSQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KNDUTqgyVuD8TfoHXnVgEV","name":"mcp__github__actions_list","input":{"method":"list_workflow_runs","owner":"LCV-Ideas-Software","repo":"astrologo-android","perPage":2,"workflow_runs_filter":{"event":"workflow_dispatch"}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":626152,"output_tokens":186,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":186,"cache_read_input_tokens":626152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KNDUTqgyVuD8TfoHXnVgEV":{"method":"list_workflow_runs","owner":"LCV-Ideas-Software","repo":"astrologo-android","perPage":2,"workflow_runs_filter":{"event":"workflow_dispatch"}}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgXyRciUzaAbweZjH24qj","requestRef":"49e8864a-2b28-42a0-8779-001e5480d9a2","requestedModel":"claude-mythos-5-1","type":"assistant","uuid":"351a4750-9afa-4574-9452-67551e6c9295","timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:47:46.120Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\github-operations","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
{"parentUuid":"351a4750-9afa-4574-9452-67551e6c9295","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ec5dd05e-bec6-412b-a2bc-8a4c30296990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KNDUTqgyVuD8TfoHXnVgEV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"method\":\"list_workflow_runs\",\"workflow_runs\":{\"total_count\":55,\"workflow_runs\":[{\"actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:25Z\",\"display_title\":\"Publish to Google Play\",\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"head_branch\":\"main\",\"head_commit\":{\"message\":\"Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing (#170)\\n\\n* Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing\\n\\nFirst stable release by operator decision of 30/10/2026, after the first real\\nweb purchase was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20).\\n\\nBackend:\\n- reconcileSweep: an unpaid CHECKOUT_READY/PAYMENT_PENDING order whose\\n  authoritative read answers a definitive 4xx (not 429) and that holds no\\n  entitlement moves to ABANDONED (manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING,\\n  nextRereadAt null) instead of being deferred every minute; new\\n  observeMissing hook logs payment_order_missing_at_provider from V2Host.\\n  429 and 5xx remain transient. Two ORDTST orders of 27/10/2026 answering\\n  404 order_not_found motivated it (LCV-464).\\n- NativeMercadoPagoOrders.request: every provider call carries the official\\n  SDK identification (User-Agent MercadoPago Java SDK/<CURRENT_VERSION>,\\n  X-Product-Id, X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig), as\\n  MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders does for the SDK-serialized creation.\\n- Tests: unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever,\\n  everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification.\\n\\nApp and Play:\\n- versionCode 21, versionName 1.0.0; CHANGELOG and README.\\n- play/listings pt-BR and en-US: product presentation (short 78 chars, full\\n  2758/2693 chars); release notes as the product presentation (394 chars);\\n  eight new phone screenshots (1080x1800, 24-bit RGB) from the real debug\\n  app on pixel_10_api37 in Portuguese; play/README.md records them.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Abandon only on a confirmed 404 order_not_found; keep 400/401/403 transient\\n\\nReview of PR #170 (Codex, Claude bot) and Entire trail 223 (three findings):\\nthe previous guard treated every 4xx except 429 as \\\"the provider no longer\\nknows this order\\\", so a revoked or misbound credential (401/403) or a 400\\nwould have moved every due unpaid order to ABANDONED with no further\\nreread, and a later accredited webhook would have refunded instead of\\ndelivering (MpOrderTransitions.observe → NOT_GRANTABLE).\\n\\nThe sweep now settles only on the confirmed missing-resource answer\\n(status 404 and code order_not_found); everything else keeps the transient\\npath (deferred, logged, resumed once the credential is repaired). The test\\ncovers 429, 500, 503, 400, 401, 403, a bare 404 and a 404 with another code.\\nCHANGELOG wording follows.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Shorten the settle comment and fix the observeMissing KDoc\\n\\nEntire trail 223 findings 01M65HAY1V0H and 01M65HAY1DTM on 1887209: the\\ninline comment narrated history that already lives in the CHANGELOG, and\\nthe KDoc still described the rejected \\\"any 4xx\\\" rule.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Log push_send_failed when an FCM send fails with a non-terminal error\\n\\nExecutionMessaging.send swallowed every FirebaseMessagingException other\\nthan UNREGISTERED/INVALID_ARGUMENT, so a lost \\\"ready\\\" or \\\"progress\\\" push\\nleft no trace. It now prints a structured WARNING event (type, FCM error\\ncode; no account, device or reference) that the native log-based metric\\nastrologo_push_send_failed and its alert policy count. Observability\\nitem of the 1.0.0 launch review (LCV-464).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Native staged rollout input, push_send_failed changelog, JDT resource note\\n\\n- publish-play.yml: `release_status: inProgress` with a `user_fraction`\\n  input (0 < fraction < 1) follows the official \\\"Staged Rollouts\\\" workflow\\n  (`userFraction` only with `inProgress`); the configuration step validates\\n  the fraction, PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN is required for every non-draft\\n  production run, and the GitHub Release steps run for completed and\\n  inProgress alike (both are served to users). README follows. Operator\\n  decision of 30/10/2026 (LCV-464).\\n- CHANGELOG [1.0.0]: bullets for `push_send_failed` (Entire trail 223\\n  finding 01M65J9NQ17T) and for the staged rollout input.\\n- GeminiSingleExchangeTransport: `@SuppressWarnings(\\\"resource\\\")` with the\\n  ownership note on the bounded body; Eclipse JDT flagged a leak that does\\n  not exist (closing the returned ResponseBody closes the bounded stream).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Report payment_order_missing_at_provider only when the CAS abandoned the order\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding 01M65KM7ZH4W: observeMissing ran before\\nstore.mutate, so a row changed concurrently (webhook or grant between the\\nread and the CAS) was logged as ABANDONED although nothing was abandoned.\\nThe observer now runs only when the mutate applied the transition; the\\ntest adds the concurrent-accreditation case (row stays PAID, no event).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* One source of truth for the Mercado Pago SDK identification headers\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: request() already sets User-Agent, X-Product-Id\\nand X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig, so the checkout client no longer\\nfilters the SDK's copies back in through a sdkHeaders parameter. The header\\ntest now also exercises the SDK-serialized creation (POST /v1/orders).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Observe the 404 abandonment only when this CAS produced it\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: the guard looked at the returned row's state, so\\na row another sweep had already abandoned for the same reason would be\\nreported again. A local flag set inside the mutate lambda now records\\nwhether this call produced the copy; the test adds that case.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"},\"head_sha\":\"f93e880fdb6ddc000247213403f8577e44bc2b46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/41015256076\",\"id\":41015256076,\"name\":\"Publish to Google Play\",\"path\":\".github/workflows/publish-play.yml\",\"run_attempt\":1,\"run_number\":21,\"run_started_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:25Z\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"triggering_actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:30Z\",\"workflow_id\":360856836},{\"actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:23Z\",\"display_title\":\"Deploy paid backend\",\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"head_branch\":\"main\",\"head_commit\":{\"message\":\"Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing (#170)\\n\\n* Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing\\n\\nFirst stable release by operator decision of 30/10/2026, after the first real\\nweb purchase was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20).\\n\\nBackend:\\n- reconcileSweep: an unpaid CHECKOUT_READY/PAYMENT_PENDING order whose\\n  authoritative read answers a definitive 4xx (not 429) and that holds no\\n  entitlement moves to ABANDONED (manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING,\\n  nextRereadAt null) instead of being deferred every minute; new\\n  observeMissing hook logs payment_order_missing_at_provider from V2Host.\\n  429 and 5xx remain transient. Two ORDTST orders of 27/10/2026 answering\\n  404 order_not_found motivated it (LCV-464).\\n- NativeMercadoPagoOrders.request: every provider call carries the official\\n  SDK identification (User-Agent MercadoPago Java SDK/<CURRENT_VERSION>,\\n  X-Product-Id, X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig), as\\n  MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders does for the SDK-serialized creation.\\n- Tests: unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever,\\n  everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification.\\n\\nApp and Play:\\n- versionCode 21, versionName 1.0.0; CHANGELOG and README.\\n- play/listings pt-BR and en-US: product presentation (short 78 chars, full\\n  2758/2693 chars); release notes as the product presentation (394 chars);\\n  eight new phone screenshots (1080x1800, 24-bit RGB) from the real debug\\n  app on pixel_10_api37 in Portuguese; play/README.md records them.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Abandon only on a confirmed 404 order_not_found; keep 400/401/403 transient\\n\\nReview of PR #170 (Codex, Claude bot) and Entire trail 223 (three findings):\\nthe previous guard treated every 4xx except 429 as \\\"the provider no longer\\nknows this order\\\", so a revoked or misbound credential (401/403) or a 400\\nwould have moved every due unpaid order to ABANDONED with no further\\nreread, and a later accredited webhook would have refunded instead of\\ndelivering (MpOrderTransitions.observe → NOT_GRANTABLE).\\n\\nThe sweep now settles only on the confirmed missing-resource answer\\n(status 404 and code order_not_found); everything else keeps the transient\\npath (deferred, logged, resumed once the credential is repaired). The test\\ncovers 429, 500, 503, 400, 401, 403, a bare 404 and a 404 with another code.\\nCHANGELOG wording follows.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Shorten the settle comment and fix the observeMissing KDoc\\n\\nEntire trail 223 findings 01M65HAY1V0H and 01M65HAY1DTM on 1887209: the\\ninline comment narrated history that already lives in the CHANGELOG, and\\nthe KDoc still described the rejected \\\"any 4xx\\\" rule.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Log push_send_failed when an FCM send fails with a non-terminal error\\n\\nExecutionMessaging.send swallowed every FirebaseMessagingException other\\nthan UNREGISTERED/INVALID_ARGUMENT, so a lost \\\"ready\\\" or \\\"progress\\\" push\\nleft no trace. It now prints a structured WARNING event (type, FCM error\\ncode; no account, device or reference) that the native log-based metric\\nastrologo_push_send_failed and its alert policy count. Observability\\nitem of the 1.0.0 launch review (LCV-464).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Native staged rollout input, push_send_failed changelog, JDT resource note\\n\\n- publish-play.yml: `release_status: inProgress` with a `user_fraction`\\n  input (0 < fraction < 1) follows the official \\\"Staged Rollouts\\\" workflow\\n  (`userFraction` only with `inProgress`); the configuration step validates\\n  the fraction, PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN is required for every non-draft\\n  production run, and the GitHub Release steps run for completed and\\n  inProgress alike (both are served to users). README follows. Operator\\n  decision of 30/10/2026 (LCV-464).\\n- CHANGELOG [1.0.0]: bullets for `push_send_failed` (Entire trail 223\\n  finding 01M65J9NQ17T) and for the staged rollout input.\\n- GeminiSingleExchangeTransport: `@SuppressWarnings(\\\"resource\\\")` with the\\n  ownership note on the bounded body; Eclipse JDT flagged a leak that does\\n  not exist (closing the returned ResponseBody closes the bounded stream).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Report payment_order_missing_at_provider only when the CAS abandoned the order\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding 01M65KM7ZH4W: observeMissing ran before\\nstore.mutate, so a row changed concurrently (webhook or grant between the\\nread and the CAS) was logged as ABANDONED although nothing was abandoned.\\nThe observer now runs only when the mutate applied the transition; the\\ntest adds the concurrent-accreditation case (row stays PAID, no event).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* One source of truth for the Mercado Pago SDK identification headers\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: request() already sets User-Agent, X-Product-Id\\nand X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig, so the checkout client no longer\\nfilters the SDK's copies back in through a sdkHeaders parameter. The header\\ntest now also exercises the SDK-serialized creation (POST /v1/orders).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Observe the 404 abandonment only when this CAS produced it\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: the guard looked at the returned row's state, so\\na row another sweep had already abandoned for the same reason would be\\nreported again. A local flag set inside the mutate lambda now records\\nwhether this call produced the copy; the test adds that case.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"},\"head_sha\":\"f93e880fdb6ddc000247213403f8577e44bc2b46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/41015253231\",\"id\":41015253231,\"name\":\"Deploy paid backend\",\"path\":\".github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml\",\"run_attempt\":1,\"run_number\":26,\"run_started_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:23Z\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"triggering_actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:43:30Z\",\"workflow_id\":393281258}]}}"}]},"uuid":"84391754-0e62-4fce-a2b5-d541e8d25af6","timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:47:47.690Z","toolUseResult":"{\"method\":\"list_workflow_runs\",\"workflow_runs\":{\"total_count\":55,\"workflow_runs\":[{\"actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:25Z\",\"display_title\":\"Publish to Google Play\",\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"head_branch\":\"main\",\"head_commit\":{\"message\":\"Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing (#170)\\n\\n* Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing\\n\\nFirst stable release by operator decision of 30/10/2026, after the first real\\nweb purchase was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20).\\n\\nBackend:\\n- reconcileSweep: an unpaid CHECKOUT_READY/PAYMENT_PENDING order whose\\n  authoritative read answers a definitive 4xx (not 429) and that holds no\\n  entitlement moves to ABANDONED (manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING,\\n  nextRereadAt null) instead of being deferred every minute; new\\n  observeMissing hook logs payment_order_missing_at_provider from V2Host.\\n  429 and 5xx remain transient. Two ORDTST orders of 27/10/2026 answering\\n  404 order_not_found motivated it (LCV-464).\\n- NativeMercadoPagoOrders.request: every provider call carries the official\\n  SDK identification (User-Agent MercadoPago Java SDK/<CURRENT_VERSION>,\\n  X-Product-Id, X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig), as\\n  MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders does for the SDK-serialized creation.\\n- Tests: unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever,\\n  everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification.\\n\\nApp and Play:\\n- versionCode 21, versionName 1.0.0; CHANGELOG and README.\\n- play/listings pt-BR and en-US: product presentation (short 78 chars, full\\n  2758/2693 chars); release notes as the product presentation (394 chars);\\n  eight new phone screenshots (1080x1800, 24-bit RGB) from the real debug\\n  app on pixel_10_api37 in Portuguese; play/README.md records them.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Abandon only on a confirmed 404 order_not_found; keep 400/401/403 transient\\n\\nReview of PR #170 (Codex, Claude bot) and Entire trail 223 (three findings):\\nthe previous guard treated every 4xx except 429 as \\\"the provider no longer\\nknows this order\\\", so a revoked or misbound credential (401/403) or a 400\\nwould have moved every due unpaid order to ABANDONED with no further\\nreread, and a later accredited webhook would have refunded instead of\\ndelivering (MpOrderTransitions.observe → NOT_GRANTABLE).\\n\\nThe sweep now settles only on the confirmed missing-resource answer\\n(status 404 and code order_not_found); everything else keeps the transient\\npath (deferred, logged, resumed once the credential is repaired). The test\\ncovers 429, 500, 503, 400, 401, 403, a bare 404 and a 404 with another code.\\nCHANGELOG wording follows.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Shorten the settle comment and fix the observeMissing KDoc\\n\\nEntire trail 223 findings 01M65HAY1V0H and 01M65HAY1DTM on 1887209: the\\ninline comment narrated history that already lives in the CHANGELOG, and\\nthe KDoc still described the rejected \\\"any 4xx\\\" rule.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Log push_send_failed when an FCM send fails with a non-terminal error\\n\\nExecutionMessaging.send swallowed every FirebaseMessagingException other\\nthan UNREGISTERED/INVALID_ARGUMENT, so a lost \\\"ready\\\" or \\\"progress\\\" push\\nleft no trace. It now prints a structured WARNING event (type, FCM error\\ncode; no account, device or reference) that the native log-based metric\\nastrologo_push_send_failed and its alert policy count. Observability\\nitem of the 1.0.0 launch review (LCV-464).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Native staged rollout input, push_send_failed changelog, JDT resource note\\n\\n- publish-play.yml: `release_status: inProgress` with a `user_fraction`\\n  input (0 < fraction < 1) follows the official \\\"Staged Rollouts\\\" workflow\\n  (`userFraction` only with `inProgress`); the configuration step validates\\n  the fraction, PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN is required for every non-draft\\n  production run, and the GitHub Release steps run for completed and\\n  inProgress alike (both are served to users). README follows. Operator\\n  decision of 30/10/2026 (LCV-464).\\n- CHANGELOG [1.0.0]: bullets for `push_send_failed` (Entire trail 223\\n  finding 01M65J9NQ17T) and for the staged rollout input.\\n- GeminiSingleExchangeTransport: `@SuppressWarnings(\\\"resource\\\")` with the\\n  ownership note on the bounded body; Eclipse JDT flagged a leak that does\\n  not exist (closing the returned ResponseBody closes the bounded stream).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Report payment_order_missing_at_provider only when the CAS abandoned the order\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding 01M65KM7ZH4W: observeMissing ran before\\nstore.mutate, so a row changed concurrently (webhook or grant between the\\nread and the CAS) was logged as ABANDONED although nothing was abandoned.\\nThe observer now runs only when the mutate applied the transition; the\\ntest adds the concurrent-accreditation case (row stays PAID, no event).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* One source of truth for the Mercado Pago SDK identification headers\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: request() already sets User-Agent, X-Product-Id\\nand X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig, so the checkout client no longer\\nfilters the SDK's copies back in through a sdkHeaders parameter. The header\\ntest now also exercises the SDK-serialized creation (POST /v1/orders).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Observe the 404 abandonment only when this CAS produced it\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: the guard looked at the returned row's state, so\\na row another sweep had already abandoned for the same reason would be\\nreported again. A local flag set inside the mutate lambda now records\\nwhether this call produced the copy; the test adds that case.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"},\"head_sha\":\"f93e880fdb6ddc000247213403f8577e44bc2b46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/41015256076\",\"id\":41015256076,\"name\":\"Publish to Google Play\",\"path\":\".github/workflows/publish-play.yml\",\"run_attempt\":1,\"run_number\":21,\"run_started_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:25Z\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"triggering_actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:30Z\",\"workflow_id\":360856836},{\"actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:23Z\",\"display_title\":\"Deploy paid backend\",\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"head_branch\":\"main\",\"head_commit\":{\"message\":\"Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing (#170)\\n\\n* Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing\\n\\nFirst stable release by operator decision of 30/10/2026, after the first real\\nweb purchase was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20).\\n\\nBackend:\\n- reconcileSweep: an unpaid CHECKOUT_READY/PAYMENT_PENDING order whose\\n  authoritative read answers a definitive 4xx (not 429) and that holds no\\n  entitlement moves to ABANDONED (manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING,\\n  nextRereadAt null) instead of being deferred every minute; new\\n  observeMissing hook logs payment_order_missing_at_provider from V2Host.\\n  429 and 5xx remain transient. Two ORDTST orders of 27/10/2026 answering\\n  404 order_not_found motivated it (LCV-464).\\n- NativeMercadoPagoOrders.request: every provider call carries the official\\n  SDK identification (User-Agent MercadoPago Java SDK/<CURRENT_VERSION>,\\n  X-Product-Id, X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig), as\\n  MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders does for the SDK-serialized creation.\\n- Tests: unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever,\\n  everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification.\\n\\nApp and Play:\\n- versionCode 21, versionName 1.0.0; CHANGELOG and README.\\n- play/listings pt-BR and en-US: product presentation (short 78 chars, full\\n  2758/2693 chars); release notes as the product presentation (394 chars);\\n  eight new phone screenshots (1080x1800, 24-bit RGB) from the real debug\\n  app on pixel_10_api37 in Portuguese; play/README.md records them.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Abandon only on a confirmed 404 order_not_found; keep 400/401/403 transient\\n\\nReview of PR #170 (Codex, Claude bot) and Entire trail 223 (three findings):\\nthe previous guard treated every 4xx except 429 as \\\"the provider no longer\\nknows this order\\\", so a revoked or misbound credential (401/403) or a 400\\nwould have moved every due unpaid order to ABANDONED with no further\\nreread, and a later accredited webhook would have refunded instead of\\ndelivering (MpOrderTransitions.observe → NOT_GRANTABLE).\\n\\nThe sweep now settles only on the confirmed missing-resource answer\\n(status 404 and code order_not_found); everything else keeps the transient\\npath (deferred, logged, resumed once the credential is repaired). The test\\ncovers 429, 500, 503, 400, 401, 403, a bare 404 and a 404 with another code.\\nCHANGELOG wording follows.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Shorten the settle comment and fix the observeMissing KDoc\\n\\nEntire trail 223 findings 01M65HAY1V0H and 01M65HAY1DTM on 1887209: the\\ninline comment narrated history that already lives in the CHANGELOG, and\\nthe KDoc still described the rejected \\\"any 4xx\\\" rule.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Log push_send_failed when an FCM send fails with a non-terminal error\\n\\nExecutionMessaging.send swallowed every FirebaseMessagingException other\\nthan UNREGISTERED/INVALID_ARGUMENT, so a lost \\\"ready\\\" or \\\"progress\\\" push\\nleft no trace. It now prints a structured WARNING event (type, FCM error\\ncode; no account, device or reference) that the native log-based metric\\nastrologo_push_send_failed and its alert policy count. Observability\\nitem of the 1.0.0 launch review (LCV-464).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Native staged rollout input, push_send_failed changelog, JDT resource note\\n\\n- publish-play.yml: `release_status: inProgress` with a `user_fraction`\\n  input (0 < fraction < 1) follows the official \\\"Staged Rollouts\\\" workflow\\n  (`userFraction` only with `inProgress`); the configuration step validates\\n  the fraction, PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN is required for every non-draft\\n  production run, and the GitHub Release steps run for completed and\\n  inProgress alike (both are served to users). README follows. Operator\\n  decision of 30/10/2026 (LCV-464).\\n- CHANGELOG [1.0.0]: bullets for `push_send_failed` (Entire trail 223\\n  finding 01M65J9NQ17T) and for the staged rollout input.\\n- GeminiSingleExchangeTransport: `@SuppressWarnings(\\\"resource\\\")` with the\\n  ownership note on the bounded body; Eclipse JDT flagged a leak that does\\n  not exist (closing the returned ResponseBody closes the bounded stream).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Report payment_order_missing_at_provider only when the CAS abandoned the order\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding 01M65KM7ZH4W: observeMissing ran before\\nstore.mutate, so a row changed concurrently (webhook or grant between the\\nread and the CAS) was logged as ABANDONED although nothing was abandoned.\\nThe observer now runs only when the mutate applied the transition; the\\ntest adds the concurrent-accreditation case (row stays PAID, no event).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* One source of truth for the Mercado Pago SDK identification headers\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: request() already sets User-Agent, X-Product-Id\\nand X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig, so the checkout client no longer\\nfilters the SDK's copies back in through a sdkHeaders parameter. The header\\ntest now also exercises the SDK-serialized creation (POST /v1/orders).\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Observe the 404 abandonment only when this CAS produced it\\n\\nEntire trail 223 finding: the guard looked at the returned row's state, so\\na row another sweep had already abandoned for the same reason would be\\nreported again. A local flag set inside the mutate lambda now records\\nwhether this call produced the copy; the test adds that case.\\n\\nRefs LCV-464\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"},\"head_sha\":\"f93e880fdb6ddc000247213403f8577e44bc2b46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/41015253231\",\"id\":41015253231,\"name\":\"Deploy paid backend\",\"path\":\".github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml\",\"run_attempt\":1,\"run_number\":26,\"run_started_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:38:23Z\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"triggering_actor\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\"id\":268063598,\"login\":\"lcv-leo\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/lcv-leo\"},\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:43:30Z\",\"workflow_id\":393281258}]}}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"github-mcp-server","title":"GitHub MCP Server","icons":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,REDACTED","mimeType":"image/png","theme":"light"},{"src":"data:image/png;base64,REDACTED","mimeType":"image/png","theme":"dark"}],"version":"github-mcp-server/remote-59427b793443f88795375c20cd01d8e035ecca69"}},"structuredContent":{"method":"list_workflow_runs","workflow_runs":{"total_count":55,"workflow_runs":[{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4","id":268063598,"login":"lcv-leo","profile_url":"https://github.com/lcv-leo"},"created_at":"2026-10-30T06:38:25Z","display_title":"Publish to Google Play","event":"workflow_dispatch","head_branch":"main","head_commit":{"message":"Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing (#170)\n\n* Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing\n\nFirst stable release by operator decision of 30/10/2026, after the first real\nweb purchase was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20).\n\nBackend:\n- reconcileSweep: an unpaid CHECKOUT_READY/PAYMENT_PENDING order whose\n  authoritative read answers a definitive 4xx (not 429) and that holds no\n  entitlement moves to ABANDONED (manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING,\n  nextRereadAt null) instead of being deferred every minute; new\n  observeMissing hook logs payment_order_missing_at_provider from V2Host.\n  429 and 5xx remain transient. Two ORDTST orders of 27/10/2026 answering\n  404 order_not_found motivated it (LCV-464).\n- NativeMercadoPagoOrders.request: every provider call carries the official\n  SDK identification (User-Agent MercadoPago Java SDK/<CURRENT_VERSION>,\n  X-Product-Id, X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig), as\n  MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders does for the SDK-serialized creation.\n- Tests: unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever,\n  everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification.\n\nApp and Play:\n- versionCode 21, versionName 1.0.0; CHANGELOG and README.\n- play/listings pt-BR and en-US: product presentation (short 78 chars, full\n  2758/2693 chars); release notes as the product presentation (394 chars);\n  eight new phone screenshots (1080x1800, 24-bit RGB) from the real debug\n  app on pixel_10_api37 in Portuguese; play/README.md records them.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Abandon only on a confirmed 404 order_not_found; keep 400/401/403 transient\n\nReview of PR #170 (Codex, Claude bot) and Entire trail 223 (three findings):\nthe previous guard treated every 4xx except 429 as \"the provider no longer\nknows this order\", so a revoked or misbound credential (401/403) or a 400\nwould have moved every due unpaid order to ABANDONED with no further\nreread, and a later accredited webhook would have refunded instead of\ndelivering (MpOrderTransitions.observe → NOT_GRANTABLE).\n\nThe sweep now settles only on the confirmed missing-resource answer\n(status 404 and code order_not_found); everything else keeps the transient\npath (deferred, logged, resumed once the credential is repaired). The test\ncovers 429, 500, 503, 400, 401, 403, a bare 404 and a 404 with another code.\nCHANGELOG wording follows.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Shorten the settle comment and fix the observeMissing KDoc\n\nEntire trail 223 findings 01M65HAY1V0H and 01M65HAY1DTM on 1887209: the\ninline comment narrated history that already lives in the CHANGELOG, and\nthe KDoc still described the rejected \"any 4xx\" rule.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Log push_send_failed when an FCM send fails with a non-terminal error\n\nExecutionMessaging.send swallowed every FirebaseMessagingException other\nthan UNREGISTERED/INVALID_ARGUMENT, so a lost \"ready\" or \"progress\" push\nleft no trace. It now prints a structured WARNING event (type, FCM error\ncode; no account, device or reference) that the native log-based metric\nastrologo_push_send_failed and its alert policy count. Observability\nitem of the 1.0.0 launch review (LCV-464).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Native staged rollout input, push_send_failed changelog, JDT resource note\n\n- publish-play.yml: `release_status: inProgress` with a `user_fraction`\n  input (0 < fraction < 1) follows the official \"Staged Rollouts\" workflow\n  (`userFraction` only with `inProgress`); the configuration step validates\n  the fraction, PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN is required for every non-draft\n  production run, and the GitHub Release steps run for completed and\n  inProgress alike (both are served to users). README follows. Operator\n  decision of 30/10/2026 (LCV-464).\n- CHANGELOG [1.0.0]: bullets for `push_send_failed` (Entire trail 223\n  finding 01M65J9NQ17T) and for the staged rollout input.\n- GeminiSingleExchangeTransport: `@SuppressWarnings(\"resource\")` with the\n  ownership note on the bounded body; Eclipse JDT flagged a leak that does\n  not exist (closing the returned ResponseBody closes the bounded stream).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Report payment_order_missing_at_provider only when the CAS abandoned the order\n\nEntire trail 223 finding 01M65KM7ZH4W: observeMissing ran before\nstore.mutate, so a row changed concurrently (webhook or grant between the\nread and the CAS) was logged as ABANDONED although nothing was abandoned.\nThe observer now runs only when the mutate applied the transition; the\ntest adds the concurrent-accreditation case (row stays PAID, no event).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* One source of truth for the Mercado Pago SDK identification headers\n\nEntire trail 223 finding: request() already sets User-Agent, X-Product-Id\nand X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig, so the checkout client no longer\nfilters the SDK's copies back in through a sdkHeaders parameter. The header\ntest now also exercises the SDK-serialized creation (POST /v1/orders).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Observe the 404 abandonment only when this CAS produced it\n\nEntire trail 223 finding: the guard looked at the returned row's state, so\na row another sweep had already abandoned for the same reason would be\nreported again. A local flag set inside the mutate lambda now records\nwhether this call produced the copy; the test adds that case.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>"},"head_sha":"f93e880fdb6ddc000247213403f8577e44bc2b46","html_url":"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/41015256076","id":41015256076,"name":"Publish to Google Play","path":".github/workflows/publish-play.yml","run_attempt":1,"run_number":21,"run_started_at":"2026-10-30T06:38:25Z","status":"in_progress","triggering_actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4","id":268063598,"login":"lcv-leo","profile_url":"https://github.com/lcv-leo"},"updated_at":"2026-10-30T06:38:30Z","workflow_id":360856836},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4","id":268063598,"login":"lcv-leo","profile_url":"https://github.com/lcv-leo"},"created_at":"2026-10-30T06:38:23Z","display_title":"Deploy paid backend","event":"workflow_dispatch","head_branch":"main","head_commit":{"message":"Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing (#170)\n\n* Release 1.0.0 (21): settle provider-missing orders, SDK headers on every MP call, Play listing\n\nFirst stable release by operator decision of 30/10/2026, after the first real\nweb purchase was delivered end to end on 0.3.17 (20).\n\nBackend:\n- reconcileSweep: an unpaid CHECKOUT_READY/PAYMENT_PENDING order whose\n  authoritative read answers a definitive 4xx (not 429) and that holds no\n  entitlement moves to ABANDONED (manualCase PROVIDER_RESOURCE_MISSING,\n  nextRereadAt null) instead of being deferred every minute; new\n  observeMissing hook logs payment_order_missing_at_provider from V2Host.\n  429 and 5xx remain transient. Two ORDTST orders of 27/10/2026 answering\n  404 order_not_found motivated it (LCV-464).\n- NativeMercadoPagoOrders.request: every provider call carries the official\n  SDK identification (User-Agent MercadoPago Java SDK/<CURRENT_VERSION>,\n  X-Product-Id, X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig), as\n  MercadoPagoClient.addDefaultHeaders does for the SDK-serialized creation.\n- Tests: unpaidOrderTheProviderNoLongerKnowsIsAbandonedInsteadOfDeferredForever,\n  everyProviderCallCarriesTheOfficialSdkIdentification.\n\nApp and Play:\n- versionCode 21, versionName 1.0.0; CHANGELOG and README.\n- play/listings pt-BR and en-US: product presentation (short 78 chars, full\n  2758/2693 chars); release notes as the product presentation (394 chars);\n  eight new phone screenshots (1080x1800, 24-bit RGB) from the real debug\n  app on pixel_10_api37 in Portuguese; play/README.md records them.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Abandon only on a confirmed 404 order_not_found; keep 400/401/403 transient\n\nReview of PR #170 (Codex, Claude bot) and Entire trail 223 (three findings):\nthe previous guard treated every 4xx except 429 as \"the provider no longer\nknows this order\", so a revoked or misbound credential (401/403) or a 400\nwould have moved every due unpaid order to ABANDONED with no further\nreread, and a later accredited webhook would have refunded instead of\ndelivering (MpOrderTransitions.observe → NOT_GRANTABLE).\n\nThe sweep now settles only on the confirmed missing-resource answer\n(status 404 and code order_not_found); everything else keeps the transient\npath (deferred, logged, resumed once the credential is repaired). The test\ncovers 429, 500, 503, 400, 401, 403, a bare 404 and a 404 with another code.\nCHANGELOG wording follows.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Shorten the settle comment and fix the observeMissing KDoc\n\nEntire trail 223 findings 01M65HAY1V0H and 01M65HAY1DTM on 1887209: the\ninline comment narrated history that already lives in the CHANGELOG, and\nthe KDoc still described the rejected \"any 4xx\" rule.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Log push_send_failed when an FCM send fails with a non-terminal error\n\nExecutionMessaging.send swallowed every FirebaseMessagingException other\nthan UNREGISTERED/INVALID_ARGUMENT, so a lost \"ready\" or \"progress\" push\nleft no trace. It now prints a structured WARNING event (type, FCM error\ncode; no account, device or reference) that the native log-based metric\nastrologo_push_send_failed and its alert policy count. Observability\nitem of the 1.0.0 launch review (LCV-464).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Native staged rollout input, push_send_failed changelog, JDT resource note\n\n- publish-play.yml: `release_status: inProgress` with a `user_fraction`\n  input (0 < fraction < 1) follows the official \"Staged Rollouts\" workflow\n  (`userFraction` only with `inProgress`); the configuration step validates\n  the fraction, PLAY_RELEASE_TOKEN is required for every non-draft\n  production run, and the GitHub Release steps run for completed and\n  inProgress alike (both are served to users). README follows. Operator\n  decision of 30/10/2026 (LCV-464).\n- CHANGELOG [1.0.0]: bullets for `push_send_failed` (Entire trail 223\n  finding 01M65J9NQ17T) and for the staged rollout input.\n- GeminiSingleExchangeTransport: `@SuppressWarnings(\"resource\")` with the\n  ownership note on the bounded body; Eclipse JDT flagged a leak that does\n  not exist (closing the returned ResponseBody closes the bounded stream).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Report payment_order_missing_at_provider only when the CAS abandoned the order\n\nEntire trail 223 finding 01M65KM7ZH4W: observeMissing ran before\nstore.mutate, so a row changed concurrently (webhook or grant between the\nread and the CAS) was logged as ABANDONED although nothing was abandoned.\nThe observer now runs only when the mutate applied the transition; the\ntest adds the concurrent-accreditation case (row stays PAID, no event).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* One source of truth for the Mercado Pago SDK identification headers\n\nEntire trail 223 finding: request() already sets User-Agent, X-Product-Id\nand X-Tracking-Id from MercadoPagoConfig, so the checkout client no longer\nfilters the SDK's copies back in through a sdkHeaders parameter. The header\ntest now also exercises the SDK-serialized creation (POST /v1/orders).\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Observe the 404 abandonment only when this CAS produced it\n\nEntire trail 223 finding: the guard looked at the returned row's state, so\na row another sweep had already abandoned for the same reason would be\nreported again. A local flag set inside the mutate lambda now records\nwhether this call produced the copy; the test adds that case.\n\nRefs LCV-464\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>"},"head_sha":"f93e880fdb6ddc000247213403f8577e44bc2b46","html_url":"https://github.com/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-android/actions/runs/41015253231","id":41015253231,"name":"Deploy paid backend","path":".github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml","run_attempt":1,"run_number":26,"run_started_at":"2026-10-30T06:38:23Z","status":"in_progress","triggering_actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4","id":268063598,"login":"lcv-leo","profile_url":"https://github.com/lcv-leo"},"updated_at":"2026-10-30T06:43:30Z","workflow_id":393281258}]}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"351a4750-9afa-4574-9452-67551e6c9295","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\github-operations","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
