 session.\n\nDedicate your full effort to \"deep research\" when seeking solutions to any problems encountered. Conduct an exhaustive, broad, and comprehensive investigation—consulting official documentation, forums, online communities, and the wider internet—before declaring any item as \"pending\" or a \"blocker.\" Before asking the operator for information you believe is missing, check existing records, chat logs, open/closed issues, etc.\n\nAlways prioritize the use of native, official solutions—whether from GitHub, Google, or Android (as applicable)—as well as those from approved, official third-party providers. Any resources required for the correct and fully functional implementation of these native, official, and approved solutions must be provided.\n\nAs a general rule, the use of custom modifications is prohibited. This policy may be relaxed on a case-by-case basis, subject to prior evaluation and approval by the operator.\n\nThe use of central controllers is prohibited. Each repository functions as an independent, self-contained unit. While all repositories must adhere to established Enterprise/Organization guidelines, standards, and structures, they remain independent and isolated from one another.\n\nUtilize \"ultrabrain\" (collective/expert-level problem-solving), cross-reviews (reserved for complex cases that warrant such an approach), and official documentation.\n\nYou are required to use native solutions and APIs from GitHub, Google, or Android (as applicable), or those from third-party providers approved by these platforms. Custom solutions should be used only as a last resort.\n\nWithin the scope of this work, ensure that all GitHub Projects, Discussions, and Issues—as well as Linear’s Issues, Projects, Teams, Initiatives, Cycles, and Milestones, and Entire’s Trails, Dispatches, Checkouts, and Memorys—are kept up to date, linked, cross-referenced, and synchronized. This includes ensuring the accuracy of statuses, priorities, assignees, labels, and content across all items whenever updates, links, cross-references, or synchronization are required.","reason":"Condição não satisfeita. Itens ainda rotulados como pendentes sem prova conclusiva de impossibilidade: (1) compra pela Play: a imagem android-36 google_apis_playstore só foi listada e nunca testada, e não há decisão do operador sobre outra conta de teste; (2) Conteúdo do app (IARC, público-alvo, categoria) tratado como só do Console sem consulta formal registrada ao operador sobre alternativas; (3) release 1.0.0 (21) sem leitura de PUBLISHED, a última leitura comprovada é RELEASE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_IN_REVIEW às 04:05:53 de 30/10/2026; (4) github-operations\\temp\\op-terminal mantido por exceção sem prova de que não pode ser movido; (5) scripts de uma só vez não enviados ao GitHub nem ao Linear. Comprovado no transcript: PR #170 mesclada em f93e880, execuções 41015253231 e 41015256076 com sucesso, revisões astrologo-paid-00072-juv e astrologo-paid-internal-00059-juy a 100%."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"63ecdcab-c818-4ba9-ad22-5958551bb7a0","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:06:37.064Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace","sessionId":"3815f8b0-8c60-4890-93a0-2fcc4c634f88","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glistening-tumbling-prism"}
