](reference_entire_change_selector_with_project_flag_returns_403.md)\n- [Entire: sessão na raiz do repo, Brain/Graph, nunca fabricar checkpoint, não sobrescrever 0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1; registro LCV-477](feedback_entire_integration_claude_usage.md) H\n- [Entire local = v0.12.2 + console (#2926) + idle-fallback; commit em worktree irmã condensava rollout de 5 GB do Codex (16 GB RAM); nunca `$args` como parâmetro em pwsh](project_entire_local_build_idle_fallback_patch.md) H\n- [doctor: manter 1password MCP + 4 conectores](feedback_doctor_keep_1password_mcp_and_four_connectors_even_unused.md)\n- Frases, datas e gatilhos das diretivas de 10/2026: [hub](feedback_hub_diretivas_2026_10.md)\n\n## Projetos / estado\n\n- [Oráculo: servidor faz tudo, app só recebe pronto + notificação](project_astrologo_server_does_everything_notify_when_ready.md) H · [Oráculo SEM usuários: não publicado, ninguém instalou/comprou; nunca desenhar nem perguntar por legado](feedback_oraculo_has_no_users_never_design_for_legacy_users.md) H\n- [Astrólogo pago: estado até 30/10 (1.0.0 em rascunho na Play, backend 00072, pendências do operador)](project_astrologo_paid_launch_state_2026_10_18.md) — #115 deploy GHA; paga sempre PT_BR · [fontes: peso igual; lente Jung](project_astrologo_library_licensed_astrolink_personare.md) H · [tudo no Linear/GitHub](feedback_store_all_learning_in_the_respective_issues_for_web_and_ios.md) H\n\n- [Android e iOS: estado e decisões](project_hub_android_ios.md) — distribuição, iOS, Swift, Swiss Ephemeris · [R8 sempre](feedback_every_android_version_ships_r8_optimized.md) H · [minSdk 36](project_android_apps_min_sdk_no_backward_compatibility.md) H · [iOS sem Mac local](project_ios_no_local_mac_build_and_simulator_on_github_actions.md) H · [iOS: nada até inscrição ATIVA](feedback_ios_no_development_until_apple_enrollment_active.md) H\n- [Histórico de estados concluídos](project_hub_historico.md) — 29/08 a 20/09 e encerrados de 10/2026\n- Docs: `version_control`, `infra_directives`, `app_memories_ref`, `ai_agents_files`, `user_subscription_tier`\n- [kotlin-lsp: NÃO instalar o servidor JetBrains (29/10)](feedback_kotlin_lsp_server_do_not_install.md) H\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Any claims or assertions you make must be thoroughly and irrefutably proven or demonstrated! I require concrete, irrefutable evidence for anything you label as \"pending\" or \"inconclusive.\"\n\nAlways use the date and time formats standard in Brazil. Your internal communication should always take place in your native language, but when communicating with the operator, the use of Brazilian Portuguese is mandatory.\n\nIt is strictly forbidden to infer, presume, guess, hallucinate, fabricate, or make dec… [+3420 chars]]: Condição não satisfeita. O transcript ainda contém itens rotulados como pendentes sem prova conclusiva de impossibilidade: (1) compra pela Play: a imagem android-36 google_apis_playstore foi só listada, nunca testada, e não há decisão do operador sobre outra conta de teste; (2) Conteúdo do app (IARC, público-alvo, categoria) tratado como só do Console sem consulta formal registrada ao operador sobre alternativas; (3) release 1.0.0 (21) sem leitura de PUBLISHED, a última leitura comprovada é RELEASE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_IN_REVIEW às 04:05:53 de 30/10/2026; (4) github-operations\\temp\\op-terminal mantido por exceção sem prova de que não pode ser movido; (5) scripts de uma só vez não enviados ao GitHub nem ao Linear.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-caveat>The command below was run directly in Claude Code, not sent to you as a request, and its output goes straight to the user. It's recorded here as context for later messages.</local-command-caveat>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<command-name>/goal</command-name>\n            <command-message>goal</command-message>\n            <command-args></command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-stdout>Goal active: Any claims or assertions you make must be thoroughly and irrefutably proven or demonstrated! I require concrete, irrefutable evidence for anything you label as \"pending\" or \"inconclusive.\"\n\nAlways use the date and time formats standard in Brazil. Your internal communication should always take place in your native language, but when communicating with the operator, the use of Brazilian Portuguese is mandatory.\n\nIt is strictly forbidden to infer, presume, guess, hallucinate, fabricate, or make decisions on one’s own. In the absence of data or information, it is mandatory to actively consult official documentation, forums, communities, or the Internet Archive. If it is not possible to resolve a question using these resources, the operator must be consulted.\n\nThe redundancy of procedures is strictly prohibited, absent conclusive proof that such redundancy is absolutely necessary.\n\nThe `D:` drive no longer exists. Save any materials that would otherwise be stored in `audits\\`, `deliverables\\`, or `Outros-Trabalhos\\` into a `temp\\` directory within each repository you are working on. Once the task is complete, delete this `temp\\` folder entirely, ensuring that everything which needs to be—or can be—saved is uploaded to GitHub or Linear. Repository branches/worktrees must be created exclusively within `C:\\Users\\lcvle\\lcv-workspace\\.worktrees\\`. We follow a \"zero local retention\" policy: save everything that needs to be saved to Linear/GitHub, then delete it from your local machine. Assets, images, and designs may be kept in Figma or Canva, provided they are properly referenced and linked for easy retrieval.\n\nAll API credentials, keys and tokens are stored in 1Password. Open a single, persistent, hidden terminal session using `op run` and execute all commands that rely on these credentials, keys and tokens within that session.\n\nDedicate your full effort to \"deep research\" when seeking solutions to any problems encountered. Conduct an exhaustive, broad, and comprehensive investigation—consulting official documentation, forums, online communities, and the wider internet—before declaring any item as \"pending\" or a \"blocker.\" Before asking the operator for information you believe is missing, check existing records, chat logs, open/closed issues, etc.\n\nAlways prioritize the use of native, official solutions—whether from GitHub, Google, or Android (as applicable)—as well as those from approved, official third-party providers. Any resources required for the correct and fully functional implementation of these native, official, and approved solutions must be provided.\n\nAs a general rule, the use of custom modifications is prohibited. This policy may be relaxed on a case-by-case basis, subject to prior evaluation and approval by the operator.\n\nThe use of central controllers is prohibited. Each repository functions as an independent, self-contained unit. While all repositories must adhere to established Enterprise/Organization guidelines, standards, and structures, they remain independent and isolated from one another.\n\nUtilize \"ultrabrain\" (collective/expert-level problem-solving), cross-reviews (reserved for complex cases that warrant such an approach), and official documentation.\n\nYou are required to use native solutions and APIs from GitHub, Google, or Android (as applicable), or those from third-party providers approved by these platforms. Custom solutions should be used only as a last resort.\n\nWithin the scope of this work, ensure that all GitHub Projects, Discussions, and Issues—as well as Linear’s Issues, Projects, Teams, Initiatives, Cycles, and Milestones, and Entire’s Trails, Dispatches, Checkouts, and Memorys—are kept up to date, linked, cross-referenced, and synchronized. This includes ensuring the accuracy of statuses, priorities, assignees, labels, and content across all items whenever updates, links, cross-references, or synchronization are required. (42 turns)\nLast check: Condição não satisfeita. O transcript ainda contém itens rotulados como pendentes sem prova conclusiva de impossibilidade: (1) compra pela Play: a imagem android-36 google_apis_playstore foi só listada, nunca testada, e não há decisão do operador sobre outra conta de teste; (2) Conteúdo do app (IARC, público-alvo, categoria) tratado como só do Console sem consulta formal registrada ao operador sobre alternativas; (3) release 1.0.0 (21) sem leitura de PUBLISHED, a última leitura comprovada é RELEASE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_IN_REVIEW às 04:05:53 de 30/10/2026; (4) github-operations\\temp\\op-terminal mantido por exceção sem prova de que não pode ser movido; (5) scripts de uma só vez não enviados ao GitHub nem ao Linear.</local-command-stdout>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-caveat>The command below was run directly in Claude Code, not sent to you as a request, and its output goes straight to the user. It's recorded here as context for later messages.</local-command-caveat>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<command-name>/goal</command-name>\n            <command-message>goal</command-message>\n            <command-args></command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-stdout>Goal active: Any claims or assertions you make must be thoroughly and irrefutably proven or demonstrated! I require concrete, irrefutable evidence for anything you label as \"pending\" or \"inconclusive.\"\n\nAlways use the date and time formats standard in Brazil. Your internal communication should always take place in your native language, but when communicating with the operator, the use of Brazilian Portuguese is mandatory.\n\nIt is strictly forbidden to infer, presume, guess, hallucinate, fabricate, or make decisions on one’s own. In the absence of data or information, it is mandatory to actively consult official documentation, forums, communities, or the Internet Archive. If it is not possible to resolve a question using these resources, the operator must be consulted.\n\nThe redundancy of procedures is strictly prohibited, ab